import{C as e,S as t,_ as n,a as r,b as i,c as a,d as o,f as s,g as c,h as l,i as u,l as d,m as f,n as p,o as m,p as h,r as g,s as _,t as v,u as y,v as b,x,y as S}from"./students-classroom-Bu102cTU.js";import{l as C}from"./navMemory-8_9IbLRV.js";var w=`/v2/assets/students-classroom-768--P7vLPzz.webp`,T=C(),E={key:`australia`,slug:`study-in-australia`,kicker:`Study destinations · Australia`,h1:`Study in Australia`,lead:`Studying in Australia gives you an internationally recognised qualification and a life-changing experience alongside it. Universities such as the University of Melbourne, the Australian National University and the University of Sydney are known worldwide for rigorous academics, modern facilities and career-focused programmes — across business, technology, healthcare and engineering, with flexible routes from undergraduate degrees to Master's and vocational study.`,heroImg:{src:e,src768:t,alt:`Sydney Harbour and the Opera House, Australia`,w:1200,h:801},formCountry:`Australia`,sections:[{heading:`The best things about studying in Australia`,points:[{title:`Universities ranked around the world`,text:`Some of the world's best universities are in Australia, known for innovation, high-quality teaching and hands-on classes that prepare you for jobs anywhere. Australian degrees are respected everywhere, which makes you more competitive wherever you go next.`},{title:`A wide range of courses`,text:`Australia offers more than 20,000 courses across its higher education and vocational systems — engineering, IT, medicine, law, hospitality, the creative arts, agriculture, design and more. Internships and real-world projects are a big part of most degrees, because the system values theory and practice together.`},{title:`Scholarships and financial support`,text:`The Australian government and its universities offer a number of scholarships for international students, helping with tuition, living expenses and sometimes even travel. We help you find and apply for the ones that fit your profile and course.`},{title:`Work while you study`,text:`International students in Australia can work part-time during term — up to 24 hours a week — and full-time during holidays. It helps with living costs and gives you professional experience in a new country; many students find part-time work in customer service, retail, hospitality or on campus.`},{title:`Post-study work visa`,text:`The Temporary Graduate Visa (Subclass 485) lets you stay and work after your degree — for two to four years, depending on your qualification and where you study. Graduating from a regional area often means a longer work visa and an easier path to permanent residency.`},{title:`Pathways to permanent residency`,text:`Australia has clear, organised routes from study to permanent residency, especially for courses in high demand and skilled work experience. Studying in particular regions, or in fields on the skilled occupation list, improves your chances of a skilled migration visa.`},{title:`Safe, friendly and multicultural`,text:`Australia is known for a safe, high-quality life and a lively, diverse society, with students from more than 190 nations. Strong support networks and student communities in Sydney, Melbourne, Adelaide and Brisbane make it a genuinely welcoming place to land.`},{title:`Quality of life and modern infrastructure`,text:`Australia consistently ranks among the best places in the world to live. Good healthcare, public transport, parks and clean cities help students settle and do well — Melbourne and Perth are recognised as especially student-friendly.`},{title:`Internships and career support`,text:`Australian institutions build career advice, internships and industry placements into student life, and those internships often lead to full-time offers. We help you choose universities whose career services are strong in your field.`},{title:`Full student support services`,text:`Australian universities are noted for robust student support: academic help, English language instruction, counselling, housing guidance and job-search advice — so you feel comfortable, confident and ready for everything your course brings.`}]},{heading:`How HN Overseas helps you study in Australia`,bullets:[(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`One-on-one counselling.`}),` We look at your academic history, ambitions and budget to build a study plan for Australia that is yours alone — the right course, university and city.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Expert shortlisting.`}),` We narrow your choices by interest and career goal, from top universities in Sydney to affordable institutions in regional areas.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Full application support.`}),` We prepare your application materials with you, polish your SOP, and make sure your profile is presented at its best.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Visa help.`}),` Every step of the visa process, from preparing documents to submitting on time, so the approval process runs smoothly.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Scholarship help.`}),` We find and apply for scholarships, grants and financial options that match your academic and personal profile.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Pre-departure briefing.`}),` Orientation before you fly: life in Australia, academic culture, housing options, finding part-time work, and staying safe.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Help after you arrive.`}),` We stay in touch after you land — settling in, part-time work, and keeping your PR pathway on track.`]})]}],closing:{heading:`Is Australia the right place for you?`,paras:[`Globally recognised education, a high quality of life, real work and migration options after graduation, and a society that is diverse and welcoming — if that is the combination you are looking for, Australia is hard to beat. Book a free counselling session below and we will build your step-by-step plan: personalised course and university suggestions, full visa and scholarship help, and honest numbers from day one.`]}},D={key:`canada`,slug:`study-in-canada`,kicker:`Study destinations · Canada`,h1:`Study in Canada`,lead:`Canada is a world leader in higher education, offering degrees recognised all over the world across engineering, management, healthcare and the creative arts — and several of its universities are consistently ranked among the best anywhere. We help you find the right bachelor's, Master's, diploma or PG diploma for your objectives, interests and budget, and walk the whole route with you.`,heroImg:{src:x,src768:i,alt:`Toronto skyline across the harbour, Canada`,w:1200,h:847},formCountry:`Canada`,sections:[{heading:`Advantages of studying in Canada`,points:[{title:`Prestigious, and more affordable`,text:`Compared with the US or UK, Canada pairs excellent universities with lower costs. Tuition varies by programme and institution, and living costs outside Toronto and Vancouver are very reasonable — a strong education with a solid return on investment.`},{title:`Work while you study`,text:`International students can work part-time during their studies and full-time during scheduled breaks. Many programmes also include a co-op — a paid placement linked to your field — so you can build Canadian work experience, and sometimes a job offer, before you graduate.`},{title:`Work after graduation`,text:`Depending on the length of your programme, you may receive a Post-Graduation Work Permit (PGWP) for up to three years after your studies — a big advantage when you later apply for permanent status.`},{title:`A route to permanent residency`,text:`International graduates can settle in Canada through routes such as Express Entry and the Provincial Nominee Programs, and many achieve permanent residency within a few years of graduating. Canada actively seeks skilled workers, so graduates are well placed.`},{title:`Safe and welcoming`,text:`Canada is known as one of the safest countries in the world, with a welcoming, cosmopolitan society that values difference. As a student you feel supported both on and off campus.`},{title:`Healthcare and student services`,text:`Most provinces offer health insurance to international students, or make affordable private coverage easy to arrange. Colleges and universities add strong student services, from mental-health support to academic and career advice.`},{title:`Qualifications recognised worldwide`,text:`Canadian degrees and diplomas are accepted everywhere. Whether you return home, move to another country or stay in Canada, your qualification helps you compete in demanding job markets.`},{title:`Industry connections and jobs`,text:`Canada's technology, banking, healthcare, construction, energy and design sectors are strong, and institutions work closely with employers. Internships and co-op programmes are common, so you graduate with academic and real-world experience together.`},{title:`Scholarships and funding`,text:`Canada offers many scholarships and grants to international students, based on academic performance, research interests, leadership and more. With the right guidance, many students secure funding that meaningfully reduces their costs.`}]},{heading:`Study options in Canada`,paras:[`Canada gives you a lot of choice in how you study:`],bullets:[(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Bachelor's degrees`}),` — three to four years`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Master's degrees`}),` — one to two years`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Postgraduate diplomas`}),` — one to two years`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Diplomas and advanced diplomas`}),` — one to three years`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Certificate courses`}),` — six months to one year`]})]},{heading:`Popular fields and student cities`,paras:[`Popular fields include Business and Management, IT and Data Science, Engineering and Technology, Nursing and Health Care, Design and Media, Tourism and Hospitality, and Teaching and Learning. The cities students choose most:`],bullets:[(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Toronto`}),` — a financial centre with great universities and diverse neighbourhoods`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Vancouver`}),` — West Coast lifestyle, with strong arts and tech programmes`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Montreal`}),` — bilingual, inexpensive and lively`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Calgary and Edmonton`}),` — welcoming communities and growing job markets`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Ottawa`}),` — a peaceful capital with high education standards`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Waterloo`}),` — known for co-op education and its tech ecosystem`]})]},{heading:`Why study in Canada with HN Overseas`,points:[{title:`Counselling tailored to you`,text:`No one-size-fits-all advice. We learn your career objectives, academic history and finances before suggesting a country, city, university and programme.`},{title:`Shortlisting built around your career`,text:`We choose courses not only by interest but by job prospects, PGWP eligibility and PR routes — and our counsellors keep current with policy changes as they happen.`},{title:`Expert application support`,text:`From university selection to submission: SOP and LOR writing, resume building and scholarship applications, handled carefully and on time.`},{title:`Visa and pre-departure advice`,text:`We help you build a strong student visa application — paperwork, evidence of funds, letters of explanation — then organise travel, housing and settling in, so you feel ready to go.`},{title:`Clear and student-centred`,text:`We do not push colleges for commissions; we work solely for your benefit. The whole process is open, honest and focused on your long-term success, not just your admission.`},{title:`Support after you arrive`,text:`We connect you with alumni in Canada and stay available after you land, from arrival guidance to networking for your career.`}]}],closing:{heading:`Begin your journey to Canada`,paras:[`Canada's education system can give you a career, a new culture and a path to living there permanently — but it takes the right guidance, correct information and real support to get there. Book a free counselling session below and we will start your plan with clarity, care and full attention.`]}},O={key:`dubai`,slug:`study-in-dubai`,kicker:`Study destinations · Dubai, UAE`,h1:`Study in Dubai`,lead:`Choosing where to study abroad is one of the most important decisions you will ever make. Dubai offers a world-class education, a lively multicultural experience and strong job prospects in one of the safest and most forward-thinking cities on earth — close to India, with a minimal time-zone difference and easy flights home.`,heroImg:{src:l,src768:f,alt:`Dubai skyline at dusk, United Arab Emirates`,w:1200,h:801},formCountry:`UAE`,sections:[{heading:`Why Dubai works for students`,points:[{title:`World-class, accredited education`,text:`Dubai hosts branch campuses of well-known universities from across the world — including Heriot-Watt University, the University of Wollongong, BITS Pilani and the University of Dubai — held to the same academic standards as their home campuses, with degrees recognised globally. Business, engineering, data science, hospitality, media and artificial intelligence are all strongly represented, from undergraduate degrees to postgraduate and professional diplomas.`},{title:`A multicultural experience like no other`,text:`People from all over the world live in Dubai, so you learn alongside different perspectives and build a genuinely global network. Indian students in particular find a strong sense of community and cultural comfort, which makes settling in far easier.`},{title:`A smart global location`,text:`Dubai sits at the crossroads of Asia, Europe and Africa, with one of the busiest international airports in the world. Travel home, or onwards to new countries during vacations, is simple — and the small time-zone difference from India keeps you close to family.`},{title:`Safe, modern and student-friendly`,text:`Dubai is consistently ranked among the safest cities in the world, with world-class infrastructure and a clean, orderly, student-centred environment. Dedicated education zones such as Dubai Knowledge Park and Academic City add learning resources, entertainment and community, alongside student housing and modern public transport.`},{title:`Learning by doing, with real jobs around you`,text:`Dubai is a major global business centre — multinational firms, tech start-ups and regional offices across finance, logistics, hospitality, healthcare, AI and construction. University internships, industry projects, seminars and job fairs give you real-world experience while you study, and students can work part-time during the academic year and full-time during breaks.`},{title:`Affordable, with scholarships`,text:`Tuition and living costs in Dubai are lower than in the UK, USA or Australia: tuition typically runs between AED 30,000 and AED 90,000 a year. Most institutions offer flexible payment plans and scholarships for academic merit, sports, leadership or financial need.`},{title:`Student visa and Golden Visa benefits`,text:`The student visa process is quick and straightforward, and universities generally handle it for you; once enrolled, you can apply for a one-year visa, renewable annually. High-performing students may qualify for the UAE Golden Visa — five or ten years of residency without a local sponsor — letting graduates live, work, start businesses and even sponsor family members.`},{title:`Lifestyle and cultural exposure`,text:`Life in Dubai goes well beyond the classroom: the Burj Khalifa, Dubai Mall and Palm Jumeirah, desert experiences, cultural festivals, global events and international expos. The city blends elegance, entertainment and heritage into a full student life.`},{title:`An ecosystem for innovation and entrepreneurs`,text:`Free zones such as Dubai Internet City, Dubai Silicon Oasis and Knowledge Park support new businesses with full ownership, tax benefits and set-up help. Universities add innovation labs, pitch competitions and incubator programmes where you can prototype ideas and meet industry mentors, in line with the UAE's Vision 2030 knowledge-economy goals.`},{title:`A global career advantage`,text:`Graduates leave Dubai with more than a degree: cross-cultural teamwork, hands-on projects and access to multinational companies make you ready for the real world — whether you build your career in Dubai, return home, or move on to other international markets.`}]},{heading:`Why choose HN Overseas for Dubai`,points:[{title:`Free one-on-one counselling`,text:`We establish whether you are eligible, what your goals are, and which courses are right for you — before anything else.`},{title:`University shortlisting`,text:`A shortlist matched to your preferences, grades and finances, across Dubai's international branch campuses and local universities.`},{title:`Full application support`,text:`SOP, LOR, paperwork and follow-ups with the university, handled end to end.`},{title:`Visa help and pre-departure briefing`,text:`Visa guidance plus the practical side: housing, advice on daily life, and cultural orientation before you go.`},{title:`Planning after study`,text:`Advice on job search, the Golden Visa route and long-term career planning once you graduate.`}]}],closing:{heading:`Start your Dubai journey`,paras:[`Studying in Dubai gives you an education from around the world, real work experience and global job prospects, in a city that is safe, exciting and forward-thinking. Whether your goal is a business degree, an MBA, engineering, data science or hospitality, Dubai offers a place to grow, connect and succeed. Book a free consultation below and we will turn your plan into a route.`]}},k={key:`europe`,slug:`study-in-europe`,kicker:`Study destinations · Europe`,h1:`Study in Europe`,lead:`Italy, Malta, Germany, France or Poland — Europe has something for everyone, whether your interest is art and fashion, engineering and technology, business or the health sciences, in some of the most beautiful and culturally rich landscapes in the world. With the right guidance you can combine a respected education, scholarships and strong job possibilities across the continent.`,heroImg:{src:n,src768:c,alt:`The Grand Canal in Venice, Italy`,w:1200,h:1820},formCountry:`Italy`,sections:[{heading:`Why choose Europe?`,bullets:[(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Low tuition.`}),` Public universities in Germany and Italy charge very little; Malta, Poland and France also offer good universities at modest cost.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Post-study work opportunities.`}),` Most European countries give graduates 12 to 24 months of post-study work permission to find a job.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Top universities.`}),` European universities and institutes are noted for academic excellence and research strength.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`A multicultural environment.`}),` Study with people from all over the world and build friendships across cultures.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Student visas and residency routes.`}),` Straightforward student visa routes, with strong support towards longer-term residency.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Schengen travel.`}),` Study in one country and travel across the Schengen area on your residence permit.`]})]},{heading:`Study in Italy — art, design and affordability`,paras:[`Italy is often the first choice for Indian students heading to Europe: it is affordable, culturally rich, and offers a wide range of programmes taught in English — bachelor's and Master's degrees across business, engineering, fashion, design and more, in cities such as Rome, Milan, Florence and Venice. It is also the route we know in the most detail, and the figures below are the ones we will confirm for your own shortlist, in writing.`,(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[`Italy now has its own guide on this site — `,(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`../study-in-italy/`,children:`Study in Italy`}),` — with the full cost breakdown, the scholarship detail and our students' stories.`]})],bullets:[(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Near-zero tuition.`}),` Public universities charge an enrolment fee of just €16 to €500 — there is effectively no tuition fee on top.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Regional scholarships (DSU).`}),` Need-based regional scholarships pay around €7,000 to €8,000 a year, alongside hostel and meal support, for eligible students.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`A known total budget.`}),` The full route typically totals ₹3 to 3.5 lakh for a Bachelor's or Master's (₹4 to 4.5 lakh for MBBS). The visa fund is separate: it is money you must show in your bank account for the visa — you don't pay it to us or to the university.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`One September intake.`}),` For the 100% scholarship route there is a single September intake each year, so the timeline is planned backwards from it.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Work while you study.`}),` 20 hours a week during your studies, full-time in the holidays.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Stay back and travel.`}),` A one-year post-study stay-back to look for work, and travel across 29 Schengen countries on your residence permit.`]})]},{heading:`HN Overseas students in Italy`,stories:[{route:`University of Milan, Italy`,name:`Mohammed Areeb`,text:`Areeb finished Class 12 at Lucknow Public School and now studies at the University of Milan on a 100% scholarship.`,hand:`100% scholarship`},{route:`University of Venice, Italy`,name:`Tejansh Singh Rathore`,text:`Tejansh holds a place at the University of Venice on a 100% scholarship.`,hand:`100% scholarship`},{route:`University of Messina, Italy`,name:`Himakshi Hada`,text:`Himakshi studies at the University of Messina on a 100% scholarship, in Sicily in the south of Italy.`,hand:`100% scholarship`},{route:`University of Cassino, Italy`,name:`Manas Sharma`,text:`Manas is studying at the University of Cassino, between Rome and Naples, through the same September intake route described above.`,hand:`September intake`}]},{heading:`Study in Malta — the English advantage in the Mediterranean`,paras:[(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[`Malta is a fast-growing favourite in the European Union: affordable, English-speaking, safe and beautiful, with a friendly student community and a low crime rate. Malta also has its own guide on this site — `,(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`../study-in-malta/`,children:`Study in Malta`}),`.`]})],bullets:[(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Language comfort.`}),` English is used widely in daily life and in teaching, so Indian students adjust quickly.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Affordable tuition and living.`}),` Among the most affordable countries in Europe on both counts.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Courses in demand.`}),` Hospitality, IT, healthcare and management lead the list.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Stay back after graduation.`}),` Graduates can apply for a one-year stay-back to explore job options.`]})]},{id:`germany`,heading:`Study in Germany — no tuition, deep technology`,paras:[`Germany offers one of the best combinations of low cost and high quality anywhere, and is a natural home for STEM students, with universities such as TU Munich, LMU Munich and Heidelberg known for precision and career-focused programmes.`],bullets:[(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`No tuition fees.`}),` Most public universities charge no tuition — only a nominal semester fee, €0 to €500 a year in our country notes.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Industry integration.`}),` Learning by doing: paid internships and research projects with major companies.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Jobs in demand.`}),` Strong openings in engineering, IT and healthcare.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Post-study work visa.`}),` Graduates can stay up to 18 months to look for work, then work towards permanent residency.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Blocked-account guidance.`}),` We help you prepare your documents (SOPs, LORs, CV) and plan the proof of funds for your blocked account.`]})]},{id:`france`,heading:`Study in France — culture, prestige and new ideas`,paras:[`France is a centre of both art and learning, with more than 1,500 programmes taught in English, so you do not need French to begin. Its leading names include the Sorbonne, INSEAD and Sciences Po.`],bullets:[(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Affordable tuition.`}),` Public universities cost €2,770 to €3,770 a year in our country notes — far less than private schools or other popular destinations.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Many different programmes.`}),` Business, fashion, the arts, hospitality, culinary studies, engineering and more.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Scholarship options.`}),` Generous schemes such as the Eiffel Excellence Programme and Charpak scholarships.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Stay back for 12 months.`}),` After graduation you can remain to look for work on special permits.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Campus France handled.`}),` We help with Campus France registration, scholarship applications and all paperwork.`]})]},{id:`poland`,heading:`Study in Poland — affordable and student-centred`,paras:[`Poland is quickly becoming a favourite for students who want a quality education at low cost, with many English-taught programmes and a strong return on investment. Recognised universities include the Jagiellonian University and the University of Warsaw.`],bullets:[(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Low tuition.`}),` Programmes run from €2,000 to €6,000 a year in our country notes.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Cheap living.`}),` Living costs are substantially lower than in Western Europe.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Work while you study.`}),` Part-time work helps cover your costs.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Stay on after graduation.`}),` Many cities and institutions allow you to stay and work after your degree.`]})]},{heading:`Europe, side by side`,table:{head:[``,`Germany`,`Italy`,`France`,`Malta`,`Poland`],rows:[[`Tuition / enrolment`,`€0–€500`,`Enrolment fee €16–€500`,`€2,770–€3,770`,`€400–€7,000`,`€2,000–€6,000`],[`Monthly living costs`,`€500–€800`,`€600–€1,000`,`€700–€1,100`,`€800–€1,200`,`€850–€1,200`],[`Teaching language`,`English and German`,`Italian and English`,`French and English`,`English`,`English and Polish`],[`Post-study work`,`18 months`,`1 year`,`12 months`,`12 months`,`Varies`],[`PR pathway`,`Yes`,`Yes`,`Yes`,`Yes`,`Yes`]]},note:`Figures for Germany, France, Malta and Poland are HN Overseas' guide figures from our country notes; Italy's are the verified figures we confirm in writing for your shortlist. Your counsellor confirms the current position for the universities you actually apply to.`},{heading:`Why HN Overseas for Europe`,points:[{title:`Counselling by country`,text:`Each European destination works differently — scholarships, funds, deadlines, visa routes. We advise country by country, based on your goals.`},{title:`Full application support`,text:`From choosing universities to writing SOPs, LORs and other documents, and managing each portal.`},{title:`Scholarship help`,text:`We identify and apply for scholarships based on need, achievement or region — including Italy's regional DSU scholarships.`},{title:`Visa and accommodation help`,text:`Visa interview preparation, paperwork and housing guidance once you are accepted.`},{title:`Support after you arrive`,text:`Alumni groups, internship leads and student networks in your new country, so you are not starting alone.`}]},{heading:`Your next steps with HN Overseas`,bullets:[(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Profile assessment`}),` — your academic history, ambitions and preferences.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`University shortlisting`}),` — a course and country matched to your profile and budget.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Application preparation`}),` — documents, essays and university portals, handled properly.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Visa processing`}),` — a full checklist and a practice interview.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Pre-departure briefing`}),` — packing, insurance, culture and what to expect on arrival.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Career planning`}),` — internships, job search and residency, planned from the start.`]})]}],closing:{heading:`Start your Europe journey`,paras:[`Studying in Europe gives you a top-quality education, a rich culture and real chances to advance your career. Germany, Italy, France, Malta and Poland are more than destinations — they are steps towards your future in the world. Book a free consultation below and we will make the route personal, simplify the complicated parts, and stay with you at every step.`]}},A={key:`nz`,slug:`study-in-new-zealand`,kicker:`Study destinations · New Zealand`,h1:`Study in New Zealand`,lead:`New Zealand is one of the best destinations right now for Indian students who want a peaceful, multicultural environment alongside a good education and real job chances after graduation. Safe, English-speaking and full of new ideas, it suits a bachelor's, a Master's or an MBA equally well — and we help you plan the whole route, not just the application.`,heroImg:{src:l,src768:f,alt:`A New Zealand harbour city beneath green hills`,w:1200,h:801},formCountry:`New Zealand`,sections:[{heading:`Why pick New Zealand?`,points:[{title:`Universities known across the world`,text:`All eight of New Zealand's universities rank among the world's best, with strong ties to business, research institutes and government — so students gain real-world experience and global recognition together.`},{title:`Practical, career-focused learning`,text:`The education system emphasises learning that is useful in the real world: critical thinking, new ideas, participatory classes, and close links to internships, industry projects and research collaboration.`},{title:`Lower fees and living costs`,text:`Compared with other English-speaking destinations, New Zealand offers lower tuition fees and living costs — in Auckland, Wellington or anywhere else in the country, the value across education, lifestyle and safety is hard to beat.`},{title:`Work while you study`,text:`International students can work up to 20 hours a week during term and full-time during breaks — local experience that also helps with living expenses.`},{title:`Post-study work visa`,text:`After your qualification you can stay for up to three years on a post-study work visa, depending on its level — time to gain international experience, apply for full-time roles and work towards permanent residency.`},{title:`Scholarships and funding`,text:`New Zealand universities and the government offer substantial scholarships to international students, from merit-based undergraduate awards to research grants for postgraduates.`},{title:`Safe, calm and friendly`,text:`New Zealand is known for safety, stable government and a low crime rate, and consistently ranks among the world's most peaceful countries — an ideal first step abroad.`},{title:`Cultures and ways of life`,text:`An open, welcoming culture with strong Indian student communities makes it easy to feel at home, in a setting that blends modern city life with rich Māori traditions.`},{title:`Adventure and natural beauty`,text:`Snow-covered mountains and glaciers, beaches, lakes and rainforests: students spend weekends hiking, skiing and exploring — good for physical and emotional health alike.`},{title:`Strong job demand`,text:`Skilled professionals are in high demand across IT, engineering, agriculture, business, healthcare and construction, improving your chances of a job, a long-term work visa or PR after graduation.`}]},{heading:`Popular courses for Indian students`,bullets:[`Business and Management (including MBA)`,`Computing and Information Technology`,`Civil, mechanical and electrical engineering`,`Hospitality and Tourism Management`,`Health Sciences and Nursing`,`Environmental Science and Agriculture`,`Arts, Design and Media`,`Data Science and AI`]},{heading:`New Zealand's universities`,bullets:[(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`University of Auckland`}),` — New Zealand's largest and highest-ranked university`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`University of Otago`}),` — known for medical and health sciences`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`University of Canterbury`}),` — a great place for engineering and research`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Victoria University of Wellington`}),` — the best place for law, humanities and government`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`University of Waikato`}),` — focused on business, computing and new ideas`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Massey University`}),` — well known for arts, agriculture and food technology`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Lincoln University`}),` — strong in life and environmental sciences`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Auckland University of Technology (AUT)`}),` — career-focused, technology-led programmes`]})]},{heading:`Who New Zealand suits`,bullets:[`Students who want an English-speaking country that doesn't cost too much`,`Students looking for a safe, friendly and varied place to learn`,`Students who want an MBA or Master's with the right to work after graduating`,`Students drawn to research and innovation in agriculture, biotech, sustainability and engineering`,`Students who care about quality of life and nature alongside academic success`]},{heading:`Jobs and PR pathways`,paras:[`New Zealand maintains a Skills Shortage List across important industries. With a post-study work visa you can lawfully stay and look for work in your field of study; many students later switch to an employer-assisted visa or apply under the Skilled Migrant Category, which leads to permanent residency.`]},{heading:`A recent HN Overseas story`,stories:[{route:`University of Auckland, New Zealand`,name:`Pihu Malhotra`,text:`Pihu received her offer for MSc Environmental Management at the University of Auckland in 2 days. She also holds an offer from the University of Queensland, ranked QS 40.`,hand:`offer in 2 days`}]},{heading:`How HN Overseas helps with New Zealand`,points:[{title:`Tailored career counselling`,text:`We match courses and universities to your academic background, job ambitions and financial position.`},{title:`University and course shortlisting`,text:`A shortlist built on rankings, scholarships, return on investment and location — not on commissions.`},{title:`SOP, LOR and application help`,text:`Powerful Statements of Purpose and Letters of Recommendation, and the whole application process handled for you.`},{title:`Visa and documentation`,text:`Guidance through the student visa application, from financial documents to interview preparation.`},{title:`After admission, before departure`,text:`Housing, travel, insurance, currency exchange, packing and getting to the airport — covered before you fly.`}],bullets:[`One-on-one counselling for every student`,`No hidden costs — 100% openness`,`Current information on the latest immigration and visa rules`,`Application tracking with a friendly team`,`Help from the beginning until you land in New Zealand`]}],closing:{heading:`Begin your journey now`,paras:[`New Zealand isn't just a destination; it's the start of a worldwide future — a friendly culture, universities that prepare you for work, and study options that let you earn while you learn. Book your free counselling session below and start the journey with a plan.`]}},j={key:`uk`,slug:`study-in-uk`,kicker:`Study destinations · United Kingdom`,h1:`Study in the UK`,lead:`The UK is where your global future starts. It remains one of the most popular destinations for overseas students, and for good reason: world-class education, cultural growth and careers that can take you all over the world. We help you make the most of it — customised support, expert advice and a smooth process from counselling to campus.`,heroImg:{src:h,src768:s,alt:`The Palace of Westminster and the Thames in London`,w:1200,h:1800},formCountry:`UK`,sections:[{heading:`Why study in the UK?`,points:[{title:`Degrees known over the world`,text:`Some of the best universities in the world are in the UK, and a UK degree is respected everywhere — a real edge in job markets abroad, with a strong mix of academic and practical value across engineering, business, healthcare and the arts.`},{title:`Less time in class`,text:`Most undergraduate programmes last three years and most Master's programmes just one. You save on tuition and living costs and start working sooner — prestigious, practical and worth the money.`},{title:`A lot of different courses`,text:`Thousands of programmes across every field, from data science to fashion management and AI to international relations — with flexible courses, multiple intakes and new specialisations.`},{title:`A multicultural student life`,text:`More than 600,000 overseas students choose the UK every year. You join a global community in a culturally rich setting, and UK universities are known for being safe, welcoming and supportive.`},{title:`Work while studying`,text:`International students can work up to 20 hours a week during term and full-time during breaks — a good way to earn, gain experience and build soft skills alongside your course.`},{title:`Work options after study`,text:`The Graduate Route lets you stay after your degree: two years for undergraduate and Master's graduates, and up to three years for PhD students — time to find a good job, gain international experience and build your career.`},{title:`Scholarships and funding`,text:`University-specific funding, government-sponsored scholarships and merit awards are all available to Indian and international students — which, combined with shorter courses, lightens the financial load considerably.`},{title:`World-class infrastructure`,text:`Sophisticated campuses, state-of-the-art labs, world-class libraries and strong industry links create an environment that supports creativity and excellence, in research and in applied learning alike.`},{title:`Healthcare and living standards`,text:`The UK offers a high standard of living, excellent public transport, and access to the National Health Service (NHS) through the health surcharge included in your visa cost — medical care at little or no extra expense.`},{title:`A launchpad for the world`,text:`The UK is a gateway to the rest of Europe, giving you the chance to travel, learn and grow. A UK education is not just about study; it is the start of a genuinely global life.`}]},{heading:`The HN Overseas advantage for the UK`,points:[{title:`Personalised counselling`,text:`We examine your academic record, professional ambitions, finances and course interests to design a study plan that fits your potential.`},{title:`University shortlisting`,text:`We help you apply to the UK universities that are ideal for you — not the ones that pay us or hold affiliations with us.`},{title:`SOPs and paperwork`,text:`A great Statement of Purpose, a planned LOR strategy and well-prepared resumes, with every important step supported.`},{title:`Visa help`,text:`Updated document checklists, interview suggestions and practice sessions, so your UK visa application is properly prepared.`},{title:`Scholarship help`,text:`We find and apply for the scholarships you may be eligible for, giving you the best chance of affording your studies.`},{title:`Before you leave, and after you arrive`,text:`Packing lists, lodging advice, airport pickup information and part-time work guidance — support that continues after your visa is approved.`}]},{heading:`Our students in the UK`,paras:[`Our students have won places at prestigious UK universities, including Russell Group universities, and gone on to work in finance, IT, healthcare, consulting and more — whether the goal was an MBA from a top business school or a Master's in Data Analytics. They are part of the 3,500+ students HN Overseas has counselled from across India.`]},{heading:`A recent HN Overseas story`,stories:[{route:`University College Birmingham, UK`,name:`Nidhi Suwalka`,text:`Nidhi is one of our students at University College Birmingham, in the UK.`,hand:`Birmingham, UK`}]},{heading:`A vision for Tier 2 and Tier 3 cities`,paras:[`Our goal at HN Overseas is to make education available to everyone, not just students in big cities. We are working to reach Tier 2 and Tier 3 cities across India, so that every student who wants to attend a top UK university can — no matter where they come from. Geography should never limit talent.`]}],closing:{heading:`Ready to start your UK journey?`,paras:[`Whether you are just beginning to look at your options or ready to apply, we are here at every step. Book a free counselling session below and start your journey to studying in the UK with a plan built around you.`]}},M={key:`usa`,slug:`study-in-usa`,kicker:`Study destinations · United States`,h1:`Study in the USA`,lead:`Studying in the US is about more than receiving a degree — it is about building connections around the world. Whether your goal is a top-ranked university, a competitive MBA or a specialised STEM course, the USA offers the strongest possibilities in every subject, and our team gives Indian students straightforward, compassionate and confident guidance through the American system.`,heroImg:{src:o,src768:y,alt:`New York City skyline, United States`,w:1200,h:800},formCountry:`USA`,sections:[{heading:`Why choose the USA?`,paras:[`The US has more than 5,000 colleges and universities, many of them known all over the world. It is recognised for high academic standards, frontier technology and pioneering research, with modern infrastructure, adaptable curriculums and programmes that meet industry needs. Through internships, real-world projects and hands-on learning, you can customise your education and explore across disciplines — the American system encourages independence, creativity and critical thinking, all crucial abilities for your future career.`],points:[{title:`Top-ranked universities`,text:`Degrees from colleges known worldwide, across business, engineering, IT, healthcare, the liberal arts and more.`},{title:`Career-focused programmes`,text:`Strong career services, career fairs and deep university–industry connections that give you an edge in the job market.`},{title:`Work through OPT and CPT`,text:`STEM and other graduates can train and work during and after their studies through Optional Practical Training (OPT) and Curricular Practical Training (CPT).`},{title:`A diverse, welcoming culture`,text:`Dynamic, diverse campuses — students from all over the world are welcome in the United States, wherever they come from.`},{title:`Global networking`,text:`Relationships with students, alumni and professors from around the world that last a lifetime.`},{title:`Language and communication`,text:`Studying in an English-speaking country sharpens your communication, builds confidence and improves your employability anywhere in the world.`},{title:`Financial help and scholarships`,text:`US colleges award substantial scholarships, research assistantships and merit-based aid to international students.`}]},{heading:`How we work`,points:[{title:`Profile evaluation`,text:`One-on-one support to understand your academic background, finances, goals and preferred destinations — structured and student-centred from the start.`},{title:`Course and university shortlisting`,text:`We pick the best-fit colleges for your school and career goals, whether that is a public university or an Ivy League school.`},{title:`Tests and documents`,text:`Help with IELTS, TOEFL, GRE and GMAT preparation routes, and with your SOPs, LORs and CV.`},{title:`Application management`,text:`Our team handles the paperwork, forms, fee tracking and deadlines across every application.`},{title:`Visa help`,text:`Full guidance on the US F-1 student visa — DS-160 forms, the SEVIS fee, documentation and interview preparation.`},{title:`Pre-departure help`,text:`Travel arrangements, housing, health insurance and cultural orientation, so your onboarding is smooth.`}]},{heading:`Why HN Overseas is the right partner`,bullets:[(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Dedicated mentors.`}),` One-on-one help from your first meeting until you leave for the US.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`100% clear guidance.`}),` No promises that can't be kept — honest, ethical advice and plans of action.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Experience at every level.`}),` Undergraduates, graduates and MBA applicants all find the right US education path with us.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`India-based, pan-India reach.`}),` We are based in India and building our presence online, with in-person centres in Tier 2 cities planned in the near future.`]})],paras:[`Our goal is to be the most trusted education consultancy in India and around the world — helping students reach their goals with strategy, ethics and care. We don't just send you to study abroad; we help you get ready to do well there.`]}],closing:{heading:`Begin now`,paras:[`From business schools to Ivy League colleges, from New York to California — this is where your US adventure starts. Book your free US study consultation below and we will map the route with you.`]}},N={key:`mba`,slug:`mba-abroad`,kicker:`Programmes · MBA`,h1:`MBA Abroad`,lead:`An MBA abroad is about more than a degree. It is a way to change your life, start a career across the world and become a better leader. Whether your destination is Silicon Valley, London's financial hub, Berlin's start-up sector or Australia's business hotspots, we help you reach it with accuracy and purpose.`,heroImg:{src:d,src768:a,alt:`Students working together over a laptop in a university library`,w:1200,h:800},sections:[{heading:`Our mission`,paras:[`Our mission is simple but strong: to help Indian students become leaders in the world of work. We don't just want to get you admitted; we want to help you become a leader, thinker and change-maker in the real world. Our aim is to help more than 1,000 MBA students reach top universities in the US, UK, Australia, Germany, Ireland, New Zealand and Italy — through personalised mentoring, carefully chosen university picks and full-cycle support.`]},{heading:`What sets our MBA guidance apart`,paras:[`We specialise in MBA admissions abroad. We know what business schools look for: strong leadership ability, clear goals, outstanding academics and profiles that stand out. Our advisers work with you one-on-one to craft an application that shows how special you are.`],points:[{title:`Roadmaps built for you`,text:`Profile evaluation, school shortlisting and interview preparation — never one-size-fits-all.`},{title:`A strong university network`,text:`Connections to well-known business schools, including INSEAD, LBS, Melbourne Business School and Duke Fuqua.`},{title:`SOP and LOR writing team`,text:`Compelling, original Statements of Purpose and Letters of Recommendation that show your leadership journey and goals.`},{title:`Scholarship strategy`,text:`We help you uncover need-based and merit-based scholarships worth millions of rupees across your target schools.`},{title:`Visa, and beyond`,text:`A visa is only the first step. Pre-departure training, alumni connections and a guide for each destination get you ready for living abroad.`}]},{heading:`MBA advantages, by destination`,points:[{title:`USA`,text:`Access to top business schools such as Harvard, Columbia and Wharton — ideal for technology careers and starting your own business.`},{title:`UK`,text:`One-year MBA programmes that save time and money — a strong route for finance and consulting.`},{title:`Australia and New Zealand`,text:`Great for career switchers and for PR pathways, with schools such as UNSW and Melbourne Business School.`},{title:`Germany and Italy`,text:`A solid education at moderate cost in Europe's business centres.`},{title:`Ireland`,text:`A destination that keeps growing — a burgeoning tech economy and work rights for graduates.`}]}],closing:{heading:`Make your future global`,paras:[`Whether you want to move up in your engineering career or study business at a school like Harvard, HN Overseas is where your global MBA journey starts. Book a free consultation below and we will build your application plan.`]}},P={key:`about`,slug:`about`,kicker:`About HN Overseas`,h1:`Start your global education journey`,lead:`HN Overseas is an emerging admission consultancy with a remarkable legacy of over 35 years in the education sector. Backed by decades of experience and industry insights, we are committed to making overseas education accessible by providing expert guidance tailored to every student's aspirations and goals.`,heroImg:{src:g,src768:p,alt:`Three students talking and smiling around a table with laptops`,w:1200,h:800},sections:[{heading:`About HN Overseas`,paras:[`HN Overseas advises students and helps them select and secure admissions to the best universities abroad of their choice.`,`Our genesis lies in an urge to set standards of excellence in the quest to provide elite online education solutions to aspirants who are willing to study in renowned universities abroad. We operate on the values of integrity, transparency, and ethical behavior.`,`HN Overseas offers a full range of support services. Our objective is to have a strong 'support line' between the student and the university which makes students' study abroad journey hassle-free. We are known for our excellent services and honest consultancy. We have influential goodwill amongst the student community and are recognized for its wisdom and guidance. 'Team HN Overseas' routinely conducts seminars, workshops, and counseling sessions for students which are very well received.`,`The requirement for counseling was sensed by us in 2017 and it can be felt at present as well. Hence, many students look up to us for proper guidance, and thus we in return provided a wealth of experience and guided our students toward the best available opportunities according to their profiles.`],note:`HN Overseas in numbers: 35+ years since 1985 · 1,500+ universities · 41+ countries · 3,500+ students counselled · 98% visa success.`},{heading:`What sets HN Overseas apart`,points:[{title:`Our vision`,text:(0,T.jsx)(`span`,{className:`vm-tag`,children:`Making Global Dreams a Reality`}),more:[`We envision a world where every student has the opportunity to explore quality education beyond geographical boundaries and build a future that reflects their true potential.`,`At HN Overseas, we believe that education is more than earning a degree or securing admission to a university. It is about discovering new possibilities, gaining international exposure, developing confidence and becoming prepared for the opportunities and challenges of tomorrow.`,`Our vision is to become a trusted name in overseas education by creating a meaningful difference in every student's journey. We aspire to make international education more accessible, transparent and achievable through the right guidance, genuine advice and personalised support.`,`We want every student and family who approaches us to feel confident that they are making an informed decision. We aim to build lasting relationships based on trust, understanding and shared aspirations rather than limiting our role to the admission process.`,`As we grow, our ambition remains simple: to guide more students towards the right opportunities, connect them with institutions where they can thrive, and inspire them to think beyond boundaries.`,`Because we believe that every big achievement begins with someone who believes in your dreams.`]},{title:`Our mission`,text:(0,T.jsx)(`span`,{className:`vm-tag`,children:`Guiding Every Step. Supporting Every Dream.`}),more:[`Our mission at HN Overseas is to make the journey of studying abroad simpler, clearer and more meaningful for students and their families.`,`We understand that choosing to study in another country is a major life decision. It often comes with excitement, questions, uncertainty and many responsibilities. Every student has a different background, different ambitions and different expectations. That is why we believe there should never be a one-size-fits-all approach to overseas education.`,`We are committed to understanding each student's academic profile, interests, financial circumstances and long-term career goals before recommending suitable opportunities. Our focus is not simply on getting students into universities, but on helping them make choices that genuinely align with their future aspirations.`,`Through honest counselling, transparent communication and continuous assistance, we strive to support students throughout their journey — from the first counselling session and university selection to applications, documentation, visa guidance and pre-departure preparation.`,`We also believe that our responsibility goes beyond individual applications. By conducting educational seminars, workshops and counselling sessions, we aim to create awareness and help students make informed decisions about their academic and professional futures.`,`At every stage, we are guided by three principles:`,`Our mission is to build more than successful applications. It is to build confidence, open doors to global opportunities and create relationships that continue long after a student receives their admission letter.`,`At HN Overseas, every student is a journey, every dream deserves attention, and every opportunity deserves the right guidance.`]},{title:`Our principles`,text:(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Integrity.`}),` We believe in providing genuine advice and putting the student's interests first.`]}),more:[(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Transparency.`}),` We communicate honestly about opportunities, requirements, processes and expectations.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Commitment.`}),` We stand beside our students and provide dependable guidance throughout their overseas education journey.`]})]}]},{heading:`How we work`,paras:[`We don't use a one-size-fits-all model like other consultancies. Every student is distinct, with their own story, background and goals — and our mission is to make sure your study abroad experience is true to you.`],points:[{title:`Pathway planning just for you`,text:`We start with a long counselling session to learn your academic history, goals, budget and preferences, then narrow down the countries, universities and programmes that fit you best.`},{title:`Knowledge of high-ROI destinations`,text:`We focus on career-focused destinations — Australia, Ireland, Germany, the UK and New Zealand among them — that offer strong post-study job options and global exposure.`},{title:`Dedicated MBA Abroad help`,text:`Specific support for MBA applicants: school selection, SOPs, letters of recommendation and scholarship applications.`},{title:`Support from start to finish`,text:`From IELTS and PTE training tips to visa interviews and pre-departure briefings, we are there at every step of the journey.`},{title:`Honest, fair consulting`,text:`No empty promises. No pushing from any college. We always work for your best interests.`}]},{heading:`Our presence, and where we are growing`,paras:[`HN Overseas is based in India and growing quickly, with a strong online presence and in-person service. Our next goal is to set up satellite student support centres in Tier 2 cities, so students from smaller communities can access world-class education help. We are not only helping students get into schools abroad; we are starting a global movement of smart, career-minded students who are ready for the future.`]},{heading:`Real change, real results`,paras:[`In the last few years we have helped students from many different backgrounds study abroad and do well, as part of the 3,500+ students HN Overseas has counselled. Our alumni are our greatest achievement: engineers heading to Germany, business graduates taking MBAs in Australia, and undergraduates starting again in the US and UK. From the first call until they arrive in another country, each student gets a personal mentor, regular communication and a clear action plan.`]}],closing:{heading:`Our mission: your future`,paras:[`Studying abroad is a big decision that will change your life, and we take it very seriously. With HN Overseas you are not just applying to an institution — you are starting a new chapter, with the right people beside you at every step. Book a free consultation below and let's make your dream of a global education come true.`]}},F={key:`payment`,slug:`payment-policy`,kicker:`Policies · Payments`,h1:`Payment Policy`,lead:`Clear, student-friendly and in the open: this page explains what HN Overseas charges for, what is completely free, and how payments are made — so every student and parent understands each step before any money moves.`,sections:[{heading:`What is free`,bullets:[(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Counselling is completely free — for every country.`}),` Profile evaluation, course and country guidance, and shortlisting advice never carry a charge.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Application help is free for most countries.`}),` Where a university charges its own application fee, you pay that fee to the university — not to us.`]})]},{heading:`What carries a charge`,points:[{title:`Italy — one full process fee`,text:`Italy is handled end to end for one full process fee, covering everything from scratch to the visa, including applications to up to 3 universities. If you apply to more than 3 universities, the extra universities' application fees are yours to pay. The fee is confirmed with you in writing before any work begins.`},{title:`Ivy League — charged per application`,text:`Applications to Ivy League universities are charged per application, and the charge is confirmed with you in writing before we begin.`},{title:`Test preparation — a paid service`,text:`Coaching for GRE, GMAT, SAT, IELTS, TOEFL and PTE is a paid service, priced by course and confirmed with you before you enrol.`}]},{heading:`Official charges that stay yours`,paras:[`Small official charges — such as the visa fee, HRD attestation and registration charges — are paid by you separately, directly to the authority concerned. They are not part of any HN Overseas fee.`]},{heading:`How to pay`,paras:[`We accept payments in the following secure ways:`],bullets:[`UPI (PhonePe, Google Pay and Paytm)`,`Bank transfer (NEFT/IMPS)`,`Credit or debit card, via a payment portal`,`Cash — only at authorised HN Overseas offices`]},{heading:`Invoices and receipts`,paras:[`We issue a formal invoice and receipt for every transaction, including GST where it applies — so every payment you make to HN Overseas is documented.`]},{heading:`A warning about payments`,paras:[`Before you send any money, please verify the payment details with your counsellor. HN Overseas is not responsible for payments made to people or agents who are not authorised by us.`]},{heading:`Your financial privacy`,paras:[`HN Overseas makes sure that all payment information and personal financial information are kept safe and never shared with anyone who should not have it. We follow the rules on data privacy and use secure payment gateways to handle all transactions.`],bullets:[(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[`Refunds for our paid services are covered in our `,(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`../refund-policy/`,children:`Refund Policy`}),`.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[`How we handle your personal information is set out in our `,(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`../privacy-policy/`,children:`Privacy Policy`}),`.`]})]},{heading:`Questions about a payment`,paras:[`We are here to help. If you have any problem or question about paying or billing, contact our team at business.hnoverseas@gmail.com. We care about your trust, and we want your financial journey with us to be just as easy as your academic one.`]}]},I={key:`refund`,slug:`refund-policy`,kicker:`Policies · Refunds`,h1:`Refund Policy`,lead:`This policy covers the services HN Overseas charges for — the Italy full process fee, Ivy League per-application charges and test-preparation fees. Counselling is completely free, so there is never a counselling fee to refund. We appreciate the trust students and their families place in us, and this policy is written to be clear and fair for everyone, with students in mind first.`,sections:[{heading:`When a refund applies`,points:[{title:`Withdrawal before work starts — 90% refund`,text:`If you decide to cancel our services or withdraw your application before any work has started, you can receive a 90% refund of the amount you paid; 10% goes towards administrative costs.`},{title:`Services partly provided — pro-rated refund`,text:`If services have already started but are not finished, a pro-rated refund may be given for the portion of services not used. For example, if counselling and shortlisting are complete but the visa application has not started, a refund for the unused component is possible.`},{title:`Rejection by every shortlisted university — 50% refund`,text:`If all of the universities on your shortlist reject your application, and it is not because documents were not sent or you were not eligible, you may be able to receive a 50% refund, depending on the stage your process had reached.`},{title:`Visa denial — 30% refund`,text:`Each visa rejection is handled individually. If our team reviewed your visa application and all required documents, and the rejection is not because of any false information, we may refund 30% of the fee.`}]},{heading:`When no refund is possible`,bullets:[`If you choose to stop the process after the services have been provided`,`If documents were altered or fabricated`,`If the student did not complete their own work on time, or did not do it at all`,`If a rejection happened because academic or financial requirements were not met`]},{heading:`How to request a refund`,bullets:[(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[`Send a formal refund request by email to `,(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`business.hnoverseas@gmail.com`}),` within 15 days of cancelling the service or receiving the rejection notice.`]}),`Our team will review the request within 5 to 7 business days.`,`If approved, the refund is sent to the original payment method within 10 to 15 business days.`]}],closing:{heading:`What we promise you`,paras:[`We don't just process applications at HN Overseas; we build relationships based on honesty, dedication and mutual respect — and our refund policy is meant to show that commitment. We want people to talk to each other: if you have any question about our services or this policy, our student support team is always available to help.`]}},L={key:`privacy`,slug:`privacy-policy`,kicker:`Policies · Privacy`,h1:`Privacy Policy`,lead:`Effective date: 11 July 2025. We at HN Overseas are dedicated to safeguarding your personal information, because we recognise how important your privacy is. This Privacy Policy describes how we gather, use, retain and safeguard your data when you visit our website, www.hnoverseas.com, or use our overseas education services. We appreciate you entrusting us with your academic objectives, contact information and supporting paperwork — our goal is to help you reach the university of your dreams while maintaining the highest level of confidentiality.`,sections:[{heading:`1. Data we gather`,paras:[`We may gather the following data when you use our website or get in touch with our counselling staff:`],bullets:[(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Personal information:`}),` name, location, phone number and email address.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Academic background:`}),` test results (IELTS, GRE, GMAT, etc.), transcripts and educational credentials.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Documents submitted:`}),` resume, Statement of Purpose (SOP), Letters of Recommendation (LOR), and a copy of your passport.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Technical information:`}),` IP address, device details, browser type and cookie-based browsing activity.`]}),`This information helps us better tailor your experience and provide relevant advice about studying abroad.`]},{heading:`2. How we use your data`,paras:[`We use your information solely to help you with your study abroad experience:`],bullets:[`Matching you with appropriate programmes and universities`,`Delivering educational materials, reminders and tailored updates`,`Assisting with the application, document and visa processes`,`Improving the quality of our website and services using user behaviour`,`Contacting you for updates and consultations via phone, WhatsApp or email`,`Your information will never be sold to any parties.`]},{heading:`3. Third-party services and data sharing`,paras:[`With your permission, we may disclose your information to:`],bullets:[`Reputable university partners or representatives`,`Payment gateways (for our paid services, as described in our Payment Policy — counselling itself is always free)`,`Visa or government officials, if necessary for processing`,`Every third-party platform we use, including CRMs, analytics tools and Google Forms, complies with GDPR regulations and offers excellent data security.`]},{heading:`4. Cookies and tracking technologies`,paras:[`Cookies are used by HN Overseas to improve your online experience. Cookies help us:`],bullets:[`Recognise the most visited pages`,`Provide more individualised content to best serve you`,`Monitor the effectiveness of our campaigns (ads, SEO, etc.)`,`Your browser's functionality may be limited if you decide to disable cookies.`]},{heading:`5. Preservation of data`,paras:[`We only keep your information for as long as is required to meet your service demands or to adhere to legal obligations. You can contact us at any time to request that your data be deleted.`]},{heading:`6. Your rights`,paras:[`You are entitled to:`],bullets:[`Ask to see the personal information we have on file`,`Revise or update your data`,`Request that your data be deleted, or that its processing be limited`,`Withdraw your consent at any time`,`To make such a request, simply send us an email at business.hnoverseas@gmail.com.`]},{heading:`7. Data security`,paras:[`To safeguard your information, we implement robust security protocols, such as secure hosting, encrypted data transmission and stringent access controls. Only individuals with permission can access your data.`]},{heading:`8. Children's privacy`,paras:[`Without parental permission, our services are not meant for anyone younger than sixteen. We don't intentionally gather information from children.`]},{heading:`9. Modifications to this policy`,paras:[`This Privacy Policy may be updated periodically. This page will be updated with the effective date of any changes. You agree to such changes by using our site going forward.`]},{heading:`10. Get in touch`,paras:[`For any inquiries or concerns about this policy or the handling of your data, please get in touch with: HN Overseas Education Consultant — Email: business.hnoverseas@gmail.com · Website: www.hnoverseas.com`]}]},R={key:`terms`,slug:`terms-and-conditions`,kicker:`Policies · Terms`,h1:`Terms and Conditions`,lead:`Effective date: 11 July 2025. Welcome to HN Overseas, which we will call “Company”, “we”, “our” or “us”. These Terms and Conditions (“Terms”) explain the rules and guidelines for using our website, www.hnoverseas.com, and our services that help people study abroad. You agree to these Terms in full if you use any of our services or visit our website. Please stop using our website and services if you don't agree with these Terms.`,sections:[{heading:`1. What we want to do`,paras:[`HN Overseas helps students take bold steps toward getting an education abroad. We help those who want to study abroad in places including Australia, Ireland, Germany, Italy, the UK, the US, and New Zealand. We offer personalized solutions for undergraduate, graduate, and MBA programs.`,`Our goal is to be a clear and reliable guide for you at every step of your trip abroad, from choosing a course to getting accepted, getting a visa, and getting ready to leave.`]},{heading:`2. Who can apply and what they have to do`,paras:[`You agree to the following by using our website or services:`],bullets:[`You are at least 18 years old (or have permission from a legal guardian).`,`The information you give (such as your academic records, personal information, financial accounts, etc.) is correct and true.`,`You know that schools, consulates, and immigration laws are the ones that decide what happens with your education and visa.`,`HN Overseas can refuse to help any candidate who gives false information, breaks local or international laws, or acts unethically during the application procedure.`]},{heading:`3. What our services are`,paras:[`Here are the support services we offer:`],bullets:[`Career Counseling and Shortlisting for Colleges`,`Help with Applications for Study Abroad Programs`,`Help with MBA Admissions`,`Help with visa applications and paperwork`,`SOP (Statement of Purpose) and LOR (Letter of Recommendation) Help Before You Leave`],note:`Please be aware that HN Overseas is not an immigration agency and does not give out visas or guarantee admission to college. We help you by making the finest application possible with the information and documents you give us.`},{heading:`4. Policy on payments and refunds`,paras:[`The client must pay the agreed-upon fees in full before any paid service may commence (for example, visa submission or admittance help). You can pay with UPI, a bank transfer, or an internet gateway. These will be securely sent to you when you sign up.`],bullets:[(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[`Refunds are governed by our `,(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`../refund-policy/`,children:`Refund Policy`}),` — it sets out when a refund applies, how much is refunded and how to request one.`]})]},{heading:`5. Limits on liability`,paras:[`We do everything we can to give you accurate, up-to-date, and useful information, but we are not responsible for:`],bullets:[`Rejection of university applications or visas.`,`Changes in the rules for embassies, tuition, or immigration.`,`Actions or mistakes made by other organizations or the government.`],note:`You should check with the right embassies, colleges, and governmental channels to make sure that all final choices or legal processes are correct.`},{heading:`6. Intellectual property`,paras:[`HN Overseas owns all of the content on our website, including text, graphics, logos, and resources. You are not allowed to use, copy, or share our content for business reasons without our prior permission.`]},{heading:`7. Data and privacy use`,paras:[`Our Privacy Policy tells you how we use, keep, and safeguard your information. We gather and process your data according to this policy. You agree to this use of your data by using our services.`],bullets:[(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[`How your information may be shared — with your permission, and only as needed for your applications — is set out in our `,(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`../privacy-policy/`,children:`Privacy Policy`}),`.`]})]},{heading:`8. Changes`,paras:[`HN Overseas can change these Terms and Conditions at any moment without letting you know ahead of time. You are responsible for checking this page for the most up-to-date version.`]},{heading:`9. The law that applies`,paras:[`The laws of the Republic of India apply to these Terms. The courts in Kota, Rajasthan, India, will have the power to settle any disagreements that come up because of these Terms or the use of our services.`]},{heading:`10. Get in touch with us`,paras:[`Please don't hesitate to contact us if you have any issues about these Terms: HN Overseas — Email: business.hnoverseas@gmail.com · Website: www.hnoverseas.com`]}]},z={italy:{key:`italy`,slug:`study-in-italy`,kicker:`Study destinations · Italy`,h1:`Study in Italy`,lead:`Italy is the route we know in the most detail: 40+ public universities, an enrolment fee of €16 to €500 instead of tuition, need-based scholarships worth €7,000 to €8,000 a year for eligible students, and one September intake planned backwards from the start. The students below are studying there on 100% scholarships — this page is the full version of how that route works.`,heroImg:{src:r,src768:u,alt:`The Colosseum in Rome at dusk, lit from inside`,w:1200,h:875},formCountry:`Italy`,sections:[{heading:`Why Italy?`,bullets:[(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`40+ public universities.`}),` A wide range of programmes taught in English — bachelor's and Master's degrees across business, engineering, fashion, design and more, in cities such as Rome, Milan, Florence and Venice.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Near-zero tuition.`}),` Public universities charge an enrolment fee of just €16 to €500 — there is effectively no tuition fee on top.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`No IELTS wall.`}),` Most Italian universities accept a Medium of Instruction (MOI) certificate from your school or college instead of an English test; the visa process asks for a B2-level English certificate.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Work while you study.`}),` 20 hours a week during your studies, full-time in the holidays.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Stay back and travel.`}),` A one-year post-study stay-back to look for work, and travel across 29 Schengen countries on your residence permit.`]})]},{heading:`What it costs, honestly`,paras:[`Italy is the exception among study destinations: because its public universities charge a flat enrolment fee, the total is known upfront instead of depending on the university you pick. The full route typically totals ₹3 to 3.5 lakh for a Bachelor's or Master's degree, and ₹4 to 4.5 lakh for MBBS.`,`The visa fund is separate: it is money you must show in your bank account for the visa — you don't pay it to us or to the university. Your counsellor lays the whole figure out in writing before you commit to anything.`]},{heading:`The scholarship route`,paras:[`Need-based regional scholarships (DSU) pay around €7,000 to €8,000 a year as a stipend, alongside hostel and meal support, for eligible students — on top of the near-zero enrolment fee. For eligible students, a 100% scholarship is guaranteed.`,`There is one condition that shapes everything: for the 100% scholarship route there is a single September intake each year. Miss it and the next start is a full year later, so the timeline — profile, pre-enrolment, scholarship application and visa — is planned backwards from September, and it starts early.`]},{heading:`Our students in Italy`,stories:[{route:`University of Milan, Italy`,name:`Mohammed Areeb`,text:`Areeb finished Class 12 at Lucknow Public School and now studies at the University of Milan on a 100% scholarship.`,hand:`100% scholarship`},{route:`University of Venice, Italy`,name:`Tejansh Singh Rathore`,text:`Tejansh holds a place at the University of Venice on a 100% scholarship.`,hand:`100% scholarship`},{route:`University of Messina, Italy`,name:`Himakshi Hada`,text:`Himakshi studies at the University of Messina on a 100% scholarship, in Sicily in the south of Italy.`,hand:`100% scholarship`},{route:`University of Cassino, Italy`,name:`Manas Sharma`,text:`Manas is studying at the University of Cassino, between Rome and Naples, through the same September intake route described above.`,hand:`September intake`}]},{heading:`How HN Overseas handles Italy`,points:[{title:`One full process fee`,text:`Counselling is free, as it is for every country. For Italy, HN charges one full process fee covering everything from scratch to the visa — profile analysis, applications to up to three universities, scholarship filing, documentation and visa preparation. If you apply to more than three universities, the extra universities' own application fees are yours. The fee is confirmed in writing before you commit; small official charges such as the visa fee, HRD attestation and registration are paid by you separately.`},{title:`Profile analysed first`,text:`We are selective on this route: your profile is analysed before anything is filed, because the scholarship depends on eligibility being real, not hoped for.`},{title:`Visa file and interview practice`,text:`Your visa file is prepared document by document, and we practise the interview with you until your answers are calm, honest and clear. When students follow our documentation and guidance, our visa success rate sits between 96 and 98%.`},{title:`Support after you arrive`,text:`Pre-departure briefing, housing guidance, and student networks in Italy, so you are not starting alone.`}]}],closing:{heading:`Start your Italy journey`,paras:[`One September intake, a known total cost and a scholarship route that rewards starting early — Italy rewards families who plan ahead. Book a free consultation below and we will analyse your profile, confirm your scholarship eligibility and lay out the timeline in writing.`]}},ireland:{key:`ireland`,slug:`study-in-ireland`,kicker:`Study destinations · Ireland`,h1:`Study in Ireland`,lead:`Ireland is the English-speaking option inside the European Union: your degree is taught in English, in an EU country, with September as the one big start of the year. This guide covers the intakes and the honest cost picture — the two things that decide whether Ireland is right for you.`,heroImg:{src:S,src768:b,alt:`The Ha'penny Bridge over the River Liffey in Dublin`,w:1200,h:800},formCountry:`Ireland`,sections:[{heading:`Why Ireland?`,bullets:[(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`English-speaking, inside the EU.`}),` Your degree is taught in English and your studies sit inside the European Union — no new language to learn before you can start learning.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`September is the one big start.`}),` Every undergraduate degree and almost every Master's begins in September.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`A January option for postgraduates.`}),` A smaller January intake runs at selected universities, mainly for postgraduate courses in fields like business and computing.`]})]},{heading:`Intakes and timing`,paras:[`September is Ireland's main and fullest intake — the full range of courses opens, and applications are typically made between February and May beforehand. Most undergraduate degrees only start in September, so an Ireland plan is built early and backwards from that date.`,`January is a smaller intake at selected universities, mostly for postgraduate courses — applications run roughly September to November beforehand. If your course is one of them, January saves you waiting a full year; your counsellor confirms whether it is, in writing, before you plan around it.`]},{heading:`What it costs`,paras:[`There is no single Ireland total — the figure moves with the university, the city and the course. Dublin living costs more than Ireland's smaller cities, and fees differ course by course, so any single number printed here would mislead you.`,`What we do instead: your counsellor prices your shortlisted universities exactly — tuition, living costs, insurance and the one-time costs — free, and in writing, before you apply. Counselling itself is completely free; for Ireland our application help is free too, and you pay only the university's own application fee, if it charges one, directly to the university.`]}],closing:{heading:`Start your Ireland journey`,paras:[`An English-taught degree inside the EU, on a September timeline that rewards early planning. Book a free consultation below and we will shortlist Irish universities against your profile and budget, with every cost in writing.`]}},singapore:{key:`singapore`,slug:`study-in-singapore`,kicker:`Study destinations · Singapore`,h1:`Study in Singapore`,lead:`Singapore puts global campuses in Asia, a short flight from home: public universities with an August main intake, and private institutions and international branch campuses adding a January start. This guide covers the intakes and the honest cost picture.`,heroImg:{src:v,src768:w,alt:`Students in a seminar room at a university campus`,w:1200,h:800},formCountry:`Singapore`,sections:[{heading:`Why Singapore?`,bullets:[(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Global campuses in Asia.`}),` Public universities start in August; private institutions and international branch campuses add a January start.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Close to home.`}),` A shorter journey from India than the western destinations — travel home is part of the real cost picture we plan with you.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`August is the main start.`}),` Public universities and most private institutions begin there, so the year's planning runs backwards from August.`]})]},{heading:`Intakes and timing`,paras:[`August is Singapore's main intake — the public universities and most private institutions start then, and applications are typically made between January and March beforehand. The public-university route is competitive, so profiles are assessed early.`,`January is offered mainly by private institutions and international branch campuses, for selected undergraduate and postgraduate courses, with applications roughly September to November beforehand. Your counsellor confirms which institutions run your course in January, in writing, before you plan around it.`]},{heading:`What it costs`,paras:[`There is no single Singapore total — public universities, private institutions and branch campuses sit in different fee bands, and living costs depend on how and where you live. A single printed figure would mislead you.`,`What we do instead: your counsellor prices your shortlisted institutions exactly — tuition, living costs and the one-time costs — free, and in writing, before you apply. Counselling itself is completely free; our application help for Singapore is free too, and you pay only the institution's own application fee, if it charges one, directly to the institution.`]}],closing:{heading:`Start your Singapore journey`,paras:[`A global education in Asia, close to home, on an August timeline. Book a free consultation below and we will match Singapore institutions to your profile and budget, with every cost in writing.`]}},hungary:{key:`hungary`,slug:`study-in-hungary`,kicker:`Study destinations · Hungary`,h1:`Study in Hungary`,lead:`Hungary puts you in Budapest, in the middle of Central Europe, inside the Schengen area — at costs well below the western destinations. It is also a destination we describe carefully: there is no single Hungary calendar and no single Hungary total, and this guide says exactly how we pin both down for you.`,heroImg:{src:d,src768:a,alt:`Students laughing together over a laptop in a university library`,w:1200,h:800},formCountry:`Hungary`,sections:[{heading:`Why Hungary?`,bullets:[(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Budapest, in Central Europe.`}),` A capital city with a large student population, and the rest of the Schengen area open to you on your residence permit while you study.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Costs worked out before you apply.`}),` There is no single Hungary total — your counsellor prices your shortlisted universities exactly, free and in writing.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Intakes confirmed for your course.`}),` Start dates vary by university, so the exact intake for your course is confirmed in writing before you plan around it.`]})]},{heading:`Costs and intakes, in writing`,paras:[`Hungarian universities set their own fees and their own start dates, course by course. Rather than print a calendar or a total we cannot stand behind, we confirm both for the specific universities on your shortlist — free, and in writing — before you commit to a timeline or a budget.`,`Counselling itself is completely free, and our application help for Hungary is free too: you pay only the university's own application fee, if it charges one, directly to the university.`]}],closing:{heading:`Start your Hungary journey`,paras:[`Tell us the course you have in mind and we will come back with the universities that run it, their exact intakes and their exact costs — in writing, and free. Book a consultation below to start.`]}},malta:{key:`malta`,slug:`study-in-malta`,kicker:`Study destinations · Malta`,h1:`Study in Malta`,lead:`Malta is the English advantage in the Mediterranean: an English-speaking island inside the European Union, with tuition from €400 to €7,000 a year in our country notes and a one-year stay-back after graduation. Safe, small and friendly — this guide covers what Malta offers and how its intakes work.`,heroImg:{src:_,src768:m,alt:`A colourful Mediterranean coastal village above a harbour`,w:1200,h:1807},formCountry:`Malta`,sections:[{heading:`Why Malta?`,bullets:[(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Language comfort.`}),` English is used widely in daily life and in teaching, so Indian students adjust quickly.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Affordable tuition and living.`}),` Tuition in our country notes runs from €400 to €7,000 a year — among the most affordable in Europe on both tuition and living costs.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Courses in demand.`}),` Hospitality, IT, healthcare and management lead the list.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Stay back after graduation.`}),` Graduates can apply for a one-year stay-back to explore job options.`]}),(0,T.jsxs)(T.Fragment,{children:[(0,T.jsx)(`strong`,{children:`Safe and welcoming.`}),` A friendly student community and a low crime rate, in a small island country inside the EU.`]})]},{heading:`Costs and intakes, in writing`,paras:[`The €400 to €7,000 tuition band comes from HN's own country notes for Malta; where your course sits inside it depends on the university and the programme. Your counsellor prices your shortlisted universities exactly — free, and in writing — before you apply.`,`Malta has no single intake calendar either: start dates vary by university and course, so the exact intake for your course is confirmed in writing before you plan around it. Counselling is completely free, and our application help for Malta is free too — you pay only the university's own application fee, if it charges one, directly to the university.`]}],closing:{heading:`Start your Malta journey`,paras:[`English-taught, affordable and inside the EU — Malta suits students who want Europe without the big-city price. Book a free consultation below and we will confirm your course's intake and exact costs in writing.`]}},switzerland:{key:`switzerland`,slug:`study-in-switzerland`,kicker:`Study destinations · Switzerland`,h1:`Study in Switzerland`,lead:`World-class education, research and specialist learning in the heart of Europe. Switzerland is known for high academic standards, research, innovation and specialist education. It can be an attractive destination for students interested in engineering, technology, finance, hospitality, life sciences and international business. Students should plan carefully for the relatively high cost of living and check the country-specific entry rules for Indian qualifications.`,heroImg:{src:v,src768:w,alt:`Students in a seminar room at a university campus`,w:1200,h:800},sections:[{heading:`Why study in Switzerland?`,bullets:[`Strong reputation in research, science, engineering and innovation.`,`Internationally connected business and financial environment.`,`Renowned hospitality and tourism education.`,`Multilingual society with German-, French- and Italian-speaking regions.`,`Universities of Applied Sciences offer professionally oriented programmes.`]},{heading:`Education system and study pattern`,paras:[`Swiss higher education follows the Bologna structure, with academic and professionally oriented institutions. Programme length and admission route vary by institution and subject.`],table:{head:[`Qualification`,`Typical duration`],rows:[[`Bachelor's degree`,`Usually 3 years`],[`Master's degree`,`Usually 1–2 years`],[`Doctoral / PhD`,`Often 3–5 years`]]}},{heading:`Popular courses`,bullets:[`Business Administration, Economics and Finance`,`Hospitality and Hotel Management`,`Computer Science, Data Science and AI`,`Engineering, Robotics and Technology`,`Life Sciences and Biotechnology`,`International Relations`]},{heading:`Universities to explore`,paras:[`These institutions are starting points for research, not a ranking. Check current programme availability, campus, language of instruction, accreditation and entry requirements on the official website.`],table:{head:[`Institution`,`Key study areas`,`Official website`],rows:[[(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://ethz.ch/en.html`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`ETH Zurich`}),`Engineering, computer science, natural sciences`,(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://ethz.ch/en.html`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`https://ethz.ch/en.html`})],[(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.epfl.ch/en/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`EPFL`}),`Engineering, technology and scientific research`,(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.epfl.ch/en/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`https://www.epfl.ch/en/`})],[(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.uzh.ch/en.html`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`University of Zurich`}),`Business, economics, law and sciences`,(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.uzh.ch/en.html`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`https://www.uzh.ch/en.html`})],[(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.unige.ch/en/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`University of Geneva`}),`International relations, economics, law and sciences`,(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.unige.ch/en/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`https://www.unige.ch/en/`})],[(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.unisg.ch/en/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`University of St. Gallen`}),`Business, management, economics and finance`,(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.unisg.ch/en/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`https://www.unisg.ch/en/`})]]}},{heading:`Admission requirements: Bachelor's programmes`,bullets:[`Class 10 and 12 certificates and transcripts.`,`Recognised school-leaving qualification meeting the university's country-specific entry rules.`,`Subject prerequisites or entrance examinations, where applicable.`,`Proof of the programme language (English, German, French or Italian).`,`Indian Class 12 qualifications may not automatically provide direct entry to every Swiss Bachelor's programme; some universities specify additional requirements.`]},{heading:`Admission requirements: Master's programmes`,bullets:[`Recognised Bachelor's degree in a relevant or accepted discipline.`,`Degree certificate and complete academic transcripts.`,`CV and motivation letter or statement of purpose.`,`Proof of English or other programme-language proficiency.`,`Work experience, portfolio, GMAT/GRE or subject prerequisites where required.`],note:`Language requirements vary by institution and course. IELTS, TOEFL or other evidence may be accepted for English-taught programmes. Alternative evidence or waivers are at the institution's discretion; there is no universal waiver.`},{heading:`Tuition fees`,table:{head:[`Study category`,`Indicative annual tuition`],rows:[[`Public university tuition`,`Often around CHF 1,000–8,000+ per year, but varies by institution and international fee policy`],[`Private / specialist institutions`,`Can be substantially higher; check the institution's current fee schedule`]]}},{heading:`Cost of living`,table:{head:[`Monthly expense`,`Indicative cost`],rows:[[`Accommodation`,`CHF 700–1,200`],[`Food and groceries`,`CHF 300–500`],[`Transport`,`CHF 50–100`],[`Personal expenses`,`CHF 200–400`],[`Indicative monthly total`,`CHF 1,800–2,500`]]},note:`Estimated annual planning budget — A broad planning range is approximately CHF 22,600–38,000+ per year including tuition and living expenses. The actual budget depends heavily on the city, institution and housing. Treat this as a starting estimate and request the latest fee schedule from the institution.`},{heading:`Student visa / residence requirements for Indian students`,paras:[`Indian students generally need a national Type D visa for degree studies lasting more than 90 days. The process involves admission, preparation of financial and academic evidence, submission through the competent Swiss representation and, where applicable, review by the relevant cantonal authority. Processing time can vary.`,`Common documents may include:`],bullets:[`Valid passport and completed visa forms.`,`University admission or enrolment confirmation.`,`Proof of sufficient funds and sponsor documents, if applicable.`,`Academic certificates and transcripts.`,`Study plan, motivation letter and CV, as requested.`,`Accommodation details and health-insurance arrangements as required.`,`Photographs and any additional documents requested by the Swiss representation.`],note:`Visa and immigration reminder — The final checklist depends on nationality, course duration, institution and current immigration rules. Use the official government or embassy checklist and the university's international office instructions. Check translation, apostille/legalisation, insurance, financial threshold and appointment rules before submission.`},{heading:`Part-time work and post-study options`,bullets:[`Non-EU/EFTA students are generally subject to a waiting period before taking employment; work is commonly limited to 15 hours per week during term after the applicable initial period and authorisation.`,`Full-time work may be possible during official semester breaks, subject to rules and authorisation.`,`Graduates of Swiss higher education institutions may have a limited period to seek suitable employment, subject to eligibility and current rules.`]},{heading:`Frequently asked questions`,points:[{title:`Can Indian students study Bachelor's in Switzerland after Class 12?`,text:`Possibly, but entry rules are institution- and qualification-specific. Some universities require additional qualifications or examinations; check the selected university's India-specific criteria.`},{title:`Is Switzerland expensive for students?`,text:`Yes. Tuition at some public universities can be moderate, but accommodation, insurance and everyday living expenses are relatively high.`},{title:`Are English-taught programmes available?`,text:`Yes, particularly at Master's level, although availability differs by institution and subject. Local languages can be valuable for daily life and employment.`}]}],closing:{heading:`Is Switzerland right for you?`,paras:[`Switzerland may suit students with a strong academic profile, a realistic financial plan and an interest in specialised education, research, hospitality, finance or technology.`,`HN Overseas can support profile assessment, course and university shortlisting, application documentation, scholarship research, visa-document preparation and pre-departure planning.`]}},latvia:{key:`latvia`,slug:`study-in-latvia`,kicker:`Study destinations · Latvia`,h1:`Study in Latvia`,lead:`Explore English-taught programmes and a comparatively accessible European study destination. Latvia is a Baltic country and an EU member state offering higher education in academic and professional fields. International students consider Latvia for programmes in information technology, engineering, business, healthcare, logistics and related areas. Riga is the main higher education hub, while other cities may offer different study and living-cost options.`,heroImg:{src:d,src768:a,alt:`Students laughing together over a laptop in a university library`,w:1200,h:800},sections:[{heading:`Why study in Latvia?`,bullets:[`A range of English-taught Bachelor's and Master's programmes.`,`Comparatively manageable living costs against many Western and Northern European destinations.`,`Universities offering technology, engineering, business and health-related courses.`,`International student environment and access to the wider Baltic region.`,`Opportunities to experience European academic and cultural life.`]},{heading:`Education system and study pattern`,paras:[`Latvia follows the European higher education framework. Academic and professional programmes are offered, and programme duration depends on the qualification and field.`],table:{head:[`Qualification`,`Typical duration`],rows:[[`Bachelor's degree`,`Usually 3–4 years`],[`Master's degree`,`Usually 1–2 years`],[`Doctoral degree`,`Often 3–4 years`]]}},{heading:`Popular courses`,bullets:[`Computer Science, IT and Cybersecurity`,`Business Administration and International Business`,`Engineering and Technology`,`Data Science and Artificial Intelligence`,`Logistics and Supply Chain Management`,`Medicine, Dentistry and Health Sciences`,`Tourism and Hospitality`]},{heading:`Universities to explore`,paras:[`These institutions are starting points for research, not a ranking. Check current programme availability, campus, language of instruction, accreditation and entry requirements on the official website.`],table:{head:[`Institution`,`Key study areas`,`Official website`],rows:[[(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.lu.lv/en/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`University of Latvia`}),`Science, business, social sciences and humanities`,(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.lu.lv/en/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`https://www.lu.lv/en/`})],[(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.rtu.lv/en`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`Riga Technical University`}),`Engineering, IT, architecture and technology`,(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.rtu.lv/en`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`https://www.rtu.lv/en`})],[(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.rsu.lv/en`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`Rīga Stradiņš University`}),`Medicine, healthcare and social sciences`,(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.rsu.lv/en`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`https://www.rsu.lv/en`})],[(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.turiba.lv/en`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`Turība University`}),`Business, tourism, communication and law`,(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.turiba.lv/en`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`https://www.turiba.lv/en`})],[(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.riseba.lv/en`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`RISEBA University of Applied Sciences`}),`Business, creative industries and communication`,(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.riseba.lv/en`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`https://www.riseba.lv/en`})]]}},{heading:`Admission requirements: Bachelor's programmes`,bullets:[`Class 10 and 12 certificates and transcripts.`,`A school-leaving qualification recognised for the chosen programme.`,`English-language evidence if required by the university.`,`Passport copy and application documents.`,`Entrance examination, interview or subject prerequisites for selected courses.`]},{heading:`Admission requirements: Master's programmes`,bullets:[`Recognised Bachelor's degree in a relevant or accepted discipline.`,`Degree certificate and academic transcripts.`,`CV and motivation letter.`,`English-language proficiency evidence, if required.`,`Portfolio, interview or work experience for selected programmes.`],note:`Language requirements vary by institution and course. IELTS, TOEFL or other evidence may be accepted for English-taught programmes. Alternative evidence or waivers are at the institution's discretion; there is no universal waiver.`},{heading:`Tuition fees`,table:{head:[`Study category`,`Indicative annual tuition`],rows:[[`Business and management`,`Approximately €2,000–6,000 per year`],[`IT and computer science`,`Approximately €1,800–3,800 per year`],[`Engineering`,`Approximately €2,700–3,500 per year`],[`Medicine and healthcare`,`Can be approximately €8,000–15,000+ per year`],[`Dentistry`,`Can be approximately €15,000+ per year`]]}},{heading:`Cost of living`,table:{head:[`Monthly expense`,`Indicative cost`],rows:[[`Accommodation`,`€150–350`],[`Food and groceries`,`€150–250`],[`Transport`,`€20–50`],[`Personal expenses`,`€80–150`],[`Indicative monthly total`,`€450–700`]]},note:`Estimated annual planning budget — For many non-medical programmes, a broad planning estimate may be around €7,400–14,400 per year including tuition and living expenses. Medical and other specialist programmes can cost more. Treat this as a starting estimate and request the latest fee schedule from the institution.`},{heading:`Student visa / residence requirements for Indian students`,paras:[`The Latvian immigration route for non-EU students can involve university admission and invitation documentation, a long-stay visa and/or residence-permit formalities depending on the applicant and current procedure. Indian applicants should follow the current instructions of the Latvian Embassy and its designated service provider. Additional document verification may apply.`,`Common documents may include:`],bullets:[`Valid passport and application forms.`,`University admission, study agreement and invitation information as applicable.`,`Proof of sufficient funds and sponsor evidence, if applicable.`,`Academic certificates and transcripts.`,`Accommodation details.`,`Health insurance meeting the applicable requirements.`,`Photographs, fees and any additional documents requested by Latvian authorities.`],note:`Visa and immigration reminder — The final checklist depends on nationality, course duration, institution and current immigration rules. Use the official government or embassy checklist and the university's international office instructions. Check translation, apostille/legalisation, insurance, financial threshold and appointment rules before submission.`},{heading:`Part-time work and post-study options`,bullets:[`Student work permissions depend on the level and type of study and the conditions of the residence status.`,`Students should confirm the permitted hours and any employer or registration requirements before starting work.`,`After graduation, further stay or employment requires the appropriate immigration basis and authorisation.`]},{heading:`Frequently asked questions`,points:[{title:`Can I study in Latvia without IELTS?`,text:`Some institutions may accept alternative proof of English proficiency or conduct their own assessment. Acceptance is university- and programme-specific; there is no blanket IELTS waiver.`},{title:`Is Latvia affordable for Indian students?`,text:`It can be more affordable than several Western and Northern European destinations, but the final budget depends on tuition, accommodation and lifestyle.`},{title:`Can students work while studying?`,text:`Work rights depend on the programme and immigration status. Confirm the current conditions with the Latvian authorities and university before relying on part-time income.`}]}],closing:{heading:`Is Latvia right for you?`,paras:[`Latvia may suit students looking for English-taught programmes and a relatively manageable European living budget, particularly in IT, engineering and business. Compare programme recognition, total cost and career outcomes before choosing.`,`HN Overseas can support profile assessment, course and university shortlisting, application documentation, scholarship research, visa-document preparation and pre-departure planning.`]}},spain:{key:`spain`,slug:`study-in-spain`,kicker:`Study destinations · Spain`,h1:`Study in Spain`,lead:`Combine European education, international exposure and a vibrant student experience. Spain offers public and private higher education institutions, a wide selection of academic disciplines and a multicultural student environment. It is considered by students interested in business, tourism, engineering, technology, arts, design and social sciences. Spanish-language ability can be useful for daily life and future employment, although English-taught programmes are available, especially at postgraduate level.`,heroImg:{src:g,src768:p,alt:`Three students talking and smiling around a table with laptops`,w:1200,h:800},sections:[{heading:`Why study in Spain?`,bullets:[`Public and private university choices across different regions.`,`English-taught programmes, particularly in postgraduate study.`,`Strong academic and industry links in business, tourism, design and technology.`,`Opportunity to learn Spanish and experience a diverse culture.`,`Different city options, from major hubs to smaller university towns.`]},{heading:`Education system and study pattern`,paras:[`Spain participates in the European Higher Education Area. Official university degrees generally follow the Grado, Máster and Doctorado structure. Some professional or private programmes may use different formats.`],table:{head:[`Qualification`,`Typical duration`],rows:[[`Bachelor's (Grado)`,`Usually 4 years`],[`Master's (Máster)`,`Usually 1–2 years`],[`Doctorate (Doctorado)`,`Duration depends on full-time/part-time status and programme rules`]]}},{heading:`Popular courses`,bullets:[`International Business, Management and Finance`,`Business Analytics and Marketing`,`Computer Science, AI and Data Science`,`Engineering and Renewable Energy`,`Tourism and Hospitality Management`,`Architecture, Design and Creative Arts`,`International Relations and Sports Management`]},{heading:`Universities to explore`,paras:[`These institutions are starting points for research, not a ranking. Check current programme availability, campus, language of instruction, accreditation and entry requirements on the official website.`],table:{head:[`Institution`,`Key study areas`,`Official website`],rows:[[(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.ub.edu/web/ub/en/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`University of Barcelona`}),`Business, economics, sciences and social sciences`,(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.ub.edu/web/ub/en/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`https://www.ub.edu/web/ub/en/`})],[(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.uam.es/uam/en`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`Autonomous University of Madrid`}),`Science, business, law and social sciences`,(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.uam.es/uam/en`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`https://www.uam.es/uam/en`})],[(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.ucm.es/english`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`Complutense University of Madrid`}),`Broad range of disciplines including law, arts and sciences`,(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.ucm.es/english`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`https://www.ucm.es/english`})],[(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.uv.es/uvweb/college/en/university-valencia-1285845048380.html`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`University of Valencia`}),`Economics, science, health and social sciences`,(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.uv.es/uvweb/college/en/university-valencia-1285845048380.html`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`https://www.uv.es/uvweb/college/en/university-valencia-1285845048380.html`})],[(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.upf.edu/en/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`Pompeu Fabra University`}),`Economics, communication, social and life sciences`,(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.upf.edu/en/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`https://www.upf.edu/en/`})],[(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.ie.edu/university/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`IE University`}),`Business, management, technology and law`,(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.ie.edu/university/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`https://www.ie.edu/university/`})]]}},{heading:`Admission requirements: Bachelor's programmes`,bullets:[`Class 10 and 12 certificates and transcripts.`,`Academic recognition, equivalency or access accreditation where required.`,`Some applicants may need UNEDasiss accreditation or to meet regional/university access procedures.`,`Subject-specific entry criteria or entrance examinations, where applicable.`,`Spanish or English language proficiency according to the programme.`]},{heading:`Admission requirements: Master's programmes`,bullets:[`Recognised Bachelor's degree in a relevant or accepted discipline.`,`Degree certificate and transcripts.`,`CV and statement of purpose.`,`English or Spanish language evidence as required.`,`Recommendation letters, portfolio or work experience for selected programmes.`],note:`Language requirements vary by institution and course. IELTS, TOEFL or other evidence may be accepted for English-taught programmes. Alternative evidence or waivers are at the institution's discretion; there is no universal waiver.`},{heading:`Tuition fees`,table:{head:[`Study category`,`Indicative annual tuition`],rows:[[`Public Bachelor's programmes`,`Often approximately €700–1,700 per year, but region and non-EU fee rules vary`],[`Public Master's programmes`,`Often approximately €1,000–3,500 per year; programme and region dependent`],[`Private universities`,`Can range from several thousand euros to €20,000+ per year`]]}},{heading:`Cost of living`,table:{head:[`Monthly expense`,`Indicative cost`],rows:[[`Accommodation`,`€300–600`],[`Food and groceries`,`€180–250`],[`Transport`,`€30–60`],[`Personal expenses`,`€100–200`],[`Indicative monthly total`,`€700–1,200`]]},note:`Estimated annual planning budget — A broad public-university planning range may be approximately €9,400–17,900 per year including tuition and living expenses. Private-university tuition and costs in Madrid or Barcelona can raise the total. Treat this as a starting estimate and request the latest fee schedule from the institution.`},{heading:`Student visa / residence requirements for Indian students`,paras:[`Indian students planning studies exceeding 90 days generally need a Spanish national study visa. The application is made through the competent Spanish consular channel for the applicant's place of residence. Requirements can include admission, financial means, health insurance and, for longer stays, police and medical certificates. Check the current consular checklist and timing before applying.`,`Common documents may include:`],bullets:[`Valid passport and national visa application form.`,`Admission or acceptance letter from an eligible institution and course.`,`Evidence of tuition payment or enrolment, where required.`,`Proof of financial means and sponsor documents, if applicable.`,`Health insurance meeting Spanish requirements.`,`Academic certificates and transcripts.`,`Accommodation information, if requested.`,`For stays over 180 days, police clearance and medical certificate as required, with relevant legalisation and translation.`],note:`Visa and immigration reminder — The final checklist depends on nationality, course duration, institution and current immigration rules. Use the official government or embassy checklist and the university's international office instructions. Check translation, apostille/legalisation, insurance, financial threshold and appointment rules before submission.`},{heading:`Part-time work and post-study options`,bullets:[`Eligible study authorisations may permit work up to the applicable statutory limit, provided employment is compatible with studies and other conditions are met.`,`Internships may be included in some programmes.`,`Graduates may qualify for certain job-search or residence routes, subject to current rules and individual eligibility.`,`Spanish-language ability can improve integration and employment prospects.`]},{heading:`Frequently asked questions`,points:[{title:`Can Indian students study in Spain in English?`,text:`Yes. A range of English-taught programmes is available, especially at Master's level. Always check the actual teaching language for every module.`},{title:`Is Spain affordable for international students?`,text:`Some public university programmes and smaller cities can be comparatively affordable. Tuition varies by region and non-EU fee policy, while Madrid and Barcelona usually have higher living costs.`},{title:`Can students work while studying in Spain?`,text:`Eligible student authorisations may allow limited work subject to current immigration rules and compatibility with studies. Check the conditions printed on the authorisation and official guidance.`}]}],closing:{heading:`Is Spain right for you?`,paras:[`Spain may suit students who want a range of public and private university options, an international student environment and opportunities to develop Spanish-language skills alongside their degree.`,`HN Overseas can support profile assessment, course and university shortlisting, application documentation, scholarship research, visa-document preparation and pre-departure planning.`]}},lithuania:{key:`lithuania`,slug:`study-in-lithuania`,kicker:`Study destinations · Lithuania`,h1:`Study in Lithuania`,lead:`Discover modern European education in a growing Baltic study destination. Lithuania is an EU member state in the Baltic region with universities and colleges offering programmes in technology, engineering, business, life sciences and social sciences. International students may find English-taught programmes and a range of city environments. Applicants should compare institutional recognition, programme content, internship opportunities and the total cost of study.`,heroImg:{src:v,src768:w,alt:`Students in a seminar room at a university campus`,w:1200,h:800},sections:[{heading:`Why study in Lithuania?`,bullets:[`English-taught programmes at a number of higher education institutions.`,`Study options in IT, engineering, business, life sciences and other disciplines.`,`European higher education structure and international mobility opportunities.`,`A range of student cities, including Vilnius and Kaunas.`,`Living costs can be lower than in several Western and Northern European capitals, though costs vary.`]},{heading:`Education system and study pattern`,paras:[`Lithuanian higher education includes university and college-level studies. University studies include Bachelor's, Master's and doctoral cycles; colleges focus more on professional higher education.`],table:{head:[`Qualification`,`Typical duration`],rows:[[`Bachelor's degree`,`Usually 3–4 years`],[`Master's degree`,`Usually 1–2 years`],[`Integrated studies`,`Often 5–6 years in selected regulated fields`],[`Doctoral studies`,`Usually 4 years`]]}},{heading:`Popular courses`,bullets:[`Information Technology and Software Engineering`,`Artificial Intelligence and Data Science`,`Business, Finance and Economics`,`Mechanical and Electrical Engineering`,`Life Sciences and Biotechnology`,`Logistics and Supply Chain Management`,`Communication and Social Sciences`]},{heading:`Universities to explore`,paras:[`These institutions are starting points for research, not a ranking. Check current programme availability, campus, language of instruction, accreditation and entry requirements on the official website.`],table:{head:[`Institution`,`Key study areas`,`Official website`],rows:[[(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.vu.lt/en/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`Vilnius University`}),`Sciences, business, medicine, humanities and social sciences`,(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.vu.lt/en/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`https://www.vu.lt/en/`})],[(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://ktu.edu/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`Kaunas University of Technology`}),`Engineering, technology, IT and business`,(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://ktu.edu/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`https://ktu.edu/`})],[(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.vdu.lt/en/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`Vytautas Magnus University`}),`Humanities, social sciences, business and natural sciences`,(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.vdu.lt/en/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`https://www.vdu.lt/en/`})],[(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://vilniustech.lt/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`Vilnius Gediminas Technical University (VILNIUS TECH)`}),`Engineering, architecture, technology and business`,(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://vilniustech.lt/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`https://vilniustech.lt/`})],[(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://lsmu.lt/en/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`Lithuanian University of Health Sciences`}),`Medicine, health sciences and veterinary studies`,(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://lsmu.lt/en/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`https://lsmu.lt/en/`})]]}},{heading:`Admission requirements: Bachelor's programmes`,bullets:[`Class 10 and 12 certificates and transcripts.`,`A secondary qualification that meets the university's recognition and subject requirements.`,`English-language proficiency evidence if required.`,`Motivation letter, entrance test or interview where applicable.`,`Additional requirements for regulated courses such as medicine or other health programmes.`]},{heading:`Admission requirements: Master's programmes`,bullets:[`Recognised Bachelor's degree in a relevant discipline.`,`Degree certificate and academic transcripts.`,`CV and motivation letter.`,`English proficiency evidence where required.`,`Portfolio, interview, work experience or prerequisite subjects for selected programmes.`],note:`Language requirements vary by institution and course. IELTS, TOEFL or other evidence may be accepted for English-taught programmes. Alternative evidence or waivers are at the institution's discretion; there is no universal waiver.`},{heading:`Tuition fees`,table:{head:[`Study category`,`Indicative annual tuition`],rows:[[`Many Bachelor's programmes`,`Approximately €2,000–5,000 per year; varies by field and institution`],[`Many Master's programmes`,`Approximately €3,000–6,000 per year; varies by field and institution`],[`Medicine / specialist programmes`,`Can be significantly higher; check the exact course fee`]]}},{heading:`Cost of living`,table:{head:[`Monthly expense`,`Indicative cost`],rows:[[`Accommodation`,`€200–450`],[`Food and groceries`,`€150–250`],[`Transport`,`€10–40`],[`Personal expenses`,`€80–150`],[`Indicative monthly total`,`€500–900`]]},note:`Estimated annual planning budget — For many non-medical programmes, a broad planning range is approximately €8,000–16,800 per year including tuition and living expenses. Specialist programmes and private accommodation can increase the budget. Treat this as a starting estimate and request the latest fee schedule from the institution.`},{heading:`Student visa / residence requirements for Indian students`,paras:[`Non-EU students generally need the appropriate national visa and/or temporary residence permit for studies, depending on the length and nature of the programme and current Lithuanian procedure. The university normally provides instructions for the admission and mediation/invitation documents. Applicants should follow the current Migration Department and consular guidance.`,`Common documents may include:`],bullets:[`Valid passport and application documents.`,`Official admission or mediation/invitation information from the institution, as applicable.`,`Proof of sufficient funds and sponsor documents, if applicable.`,`Accommodation information and health insurance.`,`Academic certificates and transcripts.`,`Police certificate or other supporting documents if required.`,`Biometrics, fees and any additional documents requested by the authorities.`],note:`Visa and immigration reminder — The final checklist depends on nationality, course duration, institution and current immigration rules. Use the official government or embassy checklist and the university's international office instructions. Check translation, apostille/legalisation, insurance, financial threshold and appointment rules before submission.`},{heading:`Part-time work and post-study options`,bullets:[`International students may have work rights under the conditions attached to their study residence status; limits and exceptions can depend on study level and current law.`,`Students should confirm the current permitted work conditions before accepting employment.`,`Graduates may explore post-study residence or employment routes if they meet the relevant criteria.`]},{heading:`Frequently asked questions`,points:[{title:`Are English-taught programmes available in Lithuania?`,text:`Yes. A number of institutions offer programmes in English, but availability differs by level and subject.`},{title:`Is Lithuania a low-cost country for students?`,text:`It can be relatively affordable compared with some Western and Northern European destinations, but rent, tuition and personal lifestyle determine the real budget.`},{title:`Can I work while studying in Lithuania?`,text:`Work permissions depend on the student's immigration status, study level and current law. Verify the latest rules before relying on part-time work.`}]}],closing:{heading:`Is Lithuania right for you?`,paras:[`Lithuania may suit students seeking an EU study destination with English-taught options and a moderate budget, especially in technology, engineering and business. Check course recognition and the language needed for local employment.`,`HN Overseas can support profile assessment, course and university shortlisting, application documentation, scholarship research, visa-document preparation and pre-departure planning.`]}},netherlands:{key:`netherlands`,slug:`study-in-netherlands`,kicker:`Study destinations · Netherlands`,h1:`Study in the Netherlands`,lead:`Innovative education, international classrooms and strong links with industry. The Netherlands is a popular destination for international education, with research universities and universities of applied sciences offering a wide range of English-taught programmes. It is particularly recognised for engineering, business, logistics, agriculture, sustainability, design and technology. Students should plan early for accommodation, as housing availability can be challenging in many university cities.`,heroImg:{src:d,src768:a,alt:`Students laughing together over a laptop in a university library`,w:1200,h:800},sections:[{heading:`Why study in Netherlands?`,bullets:[`Extensive selection of English-taught programmes, particularly at Master's level.`,`Research universities and universities of applied sciences offer different learning approaches.`,`Strong links with international business, logistics, engineering and innovation.`,`Project-based and research-oriented learning approaches.`,`International student communities and a highly connected European location.`]},{heading:`Education system and study pattern`,paras:[`The Dutch system includes research universities (WO) and universities of applied sciences (HBO). Research universities are generally more academic and research-focused, while applied sciences institutions emphasise professional practice and industry-oriented learning.`],table:{head:[`Qualification`,`Typical duration`],rows:[[`Research university Bachelor's`,`Usually 3 years`],[`University of applied sciences Bachelor's`,`Usually 4 years`],[`Master's degree`,`Usually 1–2 years; some professional programmes longer`],[`Doctoral degree`,`Often 4 years, depending on appointment and research`]]}},{heading:`Popular courses`,bullets:[`Business Administration and International Management`,`Computer Science, AI and Data Science`,`Engineering and Robotics`,`Logistics and Supply Chain Management`,`Agriculture, Food Technology and Sustainability`,`Finance and Economics`,`Architecture, Design and Communication`]},{heading:`Universities to explore`,paras:[`These institutions are starting points for research, not a ranking. Check current programme availability, campus, language of instruction, accreditation and entry requirements on the official website.`],table:{head:[`Institution`,`Key study areas`,`Official website`],rows:[[(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.uva.nl/en`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`University of Amsterdam`}),`Business, social sciences, humanities and sciences`,(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.uva.nl/en`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`https://www.uva.nl/en`})],[(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.tudelft.nl/en/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`Delft University of Technology`}),`Engineering, architecture and technology`,(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.tudelft.nl/en/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`https://www.tudelft.nl/en/`})],[(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.tue.nl/en/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`Eindhoven University of Technology`}),`Engineering, computer science and innovation`,(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.tue.nl/en/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`https://www.tue.nl/en/`})],[(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.uu.nl/en`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`Utrecht University`}),`Sciences, humanities, law and social sciences`,(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.uu.nl/en`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`https://www.uu.nl/en`})],[(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.maastrichtuniversity.nl/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`Maastricht University`}),`Business, law, health and social sciences`,(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.maastrichtuniversity.nl/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`https://www.maastrichtuniversity.nl/`})],[(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.wur.nl/en.htm`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`Wageningen University & Research`}),`Agriculture, food, environment and sustainability`,(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.wur.nl/en.htm`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`https://www.wur.nl/en.htm`})]]}},{heading:`Admission requirements: Bachelor's programmes`,bullets:[`Class 10 and 12 certificates and transcripts.`,`Qualification meeting the institution's Dutch entry-level equivalence requirements; some Indian applicants may need additional qualifications.`,`Required subject background and mathematics/science prerequisites for selected courses.`,`English-language test or accepted alternative evidence.`,`Numerus fixus selection, portfolio or entrance assessment for selected programmes.`]},{heading:`Admission requirements: Master's programmes`,bullets:[`Recognised Bachelor's degree comparable to the required Dutch level.`,`Relevant academic background and prerequisite subjects.`,`Academic transcripts, CV and motivation letter.`,`English proficiency evidence, commonly IELTS/TOEFL or accepted alternatives.`,`Portfolio, references, GMAT/GRE or work experience where required.`],note:`Language requirements vary by institution and course. IELTS, TOEFL or other evidence may be accepted for English-taught programmes. Alternative evidence or waivers are at the institution's discretion; there is no universal waiver.`},{heading:`Tuition fees`,table:{head:[`Study category`,`Indicative annual tuition`],rows:[[`Non-EU Bachelor's programmes`,`Often approximately €8,000–15,000+ per year`],[`Non-EU Master's programmes`,`Often approximately €12,000–25,000+ per year`],[`Specialist / private programmes`,`May be higher; check the exact programme fee`]]}},{heading:`Cost of living`,table:{head:[`Monthly expense`,`Indicative cost`],rows:[[`Accommodation`,`€500–1,000+ (housing is competitive)`],[`Food and groceries`,`€200–350`],[`Transport`,`€50–100`],[`Insurance and personal costs`,`€150–300`],[`Indicative monthly total`,`€1,000–1,600+`]]},note:`Estimated annual planning budget — A broad planning range is approximately €20,000–44,000+ per year including tuition and living expenses. Housing availability and rent are major factors; students should arrange accommodation early and budget realistically. Treat this as a starting estimate and request the latest fee schedule from the institution.`},{heading:`Student visa / residence requirements for Indian students`,paras:[`For degree programmes, the recognised educational institution generally acts as the student's sponsor and applies for the relevant entry visa (MVV), residence permit or both, depending on nationality and circumstances. Students should follow the university's immigration office instructions and current IND requirements. Proof of funds, insurance and enrolment conditions apply.`,`Common documents may include:`],bullets:[`Valid passport and university admission/enrolment confirmation.`,`Documents requested by the university as recognised sponsor.`,`Proof of sufficient funds for living expenses and tuition as applicable.`,`Academic certificates and transcripts.`,`Health insurance arrangements appropriate to the student's status.`,`Biometrics, fees and any additional documents requested by the institution or IND.`],note:`Visa and immigration reminder — The final checklist depends on nationality, course duration, institution and current immigration rules. Use the official government or embassy checklist and the university's international office instructions. Check translation, apostille/legalisation, insurance, financial threshold and appointment rules before submission.`},{heading:`Part-time work and post-study options`,bullets:[`Non-EU students generally need a work permit arranged by the employer for paid employment and are subject to a choice between limited hours during the academic year or full-time work in June, July and August, under the applicable rules.`,`Self-employment has separate conditions; students should check official guidance before starting.`,`Eligible graduates may apply for the Dutch orientation year (zoekjaar) residence permit, subject to criteria and deadlines.`]},{heading:`Frequently asked questions`,points:[{title:`Are courses in the Netherlands taught in English?`,text:`Many programmes, especially at Master's level, are taught in English. Always check the programme language and any Dutch-language components.`},{title:`Is accommodation difficult to find?`,text:`Housing can be highly competitive in major student cities. Students should start searching as soon as they receive admission and avoid travelling without a credible accommodation plan.`},{title:`Can international students work part-time?`,text:`Yes, subject to Dutch work-permit and hour restrictions. The employer generally has to arrange the required work permit for non-EU students.`}]}],closing:{heading:`Is Netherlands right for you?`,paras:[`The Netherlands may suit students seeking English-taught programmes, research or applied learning and strong international industry exposure. It is important to have a realistic budget and secure housing before travel.`,`HN Overseas can support profile assessment, course and university shortlisting, application documentation, scholarship research, visa-document preparation and pre-departure planning.`]}},sweden:{key:`sweden`,slug:`study-in-sweden`,kicker:`Study destinations · Sweden`,h1:`Study in Sweden`,lead:`Study in an innovation-driven country with a strong focus on research and sustainability. Sweden is known for research, innovation, sustainability, technology and a collaborative learning environment. Swedish universities offer English-taught programmes, particularly at Master's level, and students can explore fields such as engineering, computer science, business, environmental studies, life sciences and design. Tuition and living costs should be planned carefully.`,heroImg:{src:g,src768:p,alt:`Three students talking and smiling around a table with laptops`,w:1200,h:800},sections:[{heading:`Why study in Sweden?`,bullets:[`Strong research and innovation ecosystem.`,`Wide range of English-taught Master's programmes.`,`Emphasis on independent thinking, teamwork and problem-solving.`,`International focus on sustainability, clean technology and life sciences.`,`Opportunities to engage with technology-led and research-intensive industries.`]},{heading:`Education system and study pattern`,paras:[`Swedish higher education follows the European higher education structure. Teaching often includes lectures, seminars, group projects, independent study and examinations. Some programmes include industry projects or thesis work.`],table:{head:[`Qualification`,`Typical duration`],rows:[[`Bachelor's degree`,`Usually 3 years`],[`Master's degree`,`Usually 1–2 years`],[`Doctoral studies`,`Often 4 years of full-time study`]]}},{heading:`Popular courses`,bullets:[`Computer Science, AI and Data Science`,`Engineering and Advanced Technology`,`Business, Economics and Management`,`Sustainability and Environmental Science`,`Renewable Energy and Clean Technology`,`Life Sciences and Biotechnology`,`Design and Interaction`]},{heading:`Universities to explore`,paras:[`These institutions are starting points for research, not a ranking. Check current programme availability, campus, language of instruction, accreditation and entry requirements on the official website.`],table:{head:[`Institution`,`Key study areas`,`Official website`],rows:[[(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.lunduniversity.lu.se/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`Lund University`}),`Engineering, sciences, business and humanities`,(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.lunduniversity.lu.se/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`https://www.lunduniversity.lu.se/`})],[(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.uu.se/en`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`Uppsala University`}),`Sciences, humanities, medicine and social sciences`,(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.uu.se/en`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`https://www.uu.se/en`})],[(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.kth.se/en`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`KTH Royal Institute of Technology`}),`Engineering, technology and architecture`,(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.kth.se/en`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`https://www.kth.se/en`})],[(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.chalmers.se/en/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`Chalmers University of Technology`}),`Engineering, technology and architecture`,(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.chalmers.se/en/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`https://www.chalmers.se/en/`})],[(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.su.se/english/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`Stockholm University`}),`Sciences, humanities, law and social sciences`,(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.su.se/english/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`https://www.su.se/english/`})],[(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.gu.se/en`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`University of Gothenburg`}),`Business, arts, sciences and social sciences`,(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.gu.se/en`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`https://www.gu.se/en`})]]}},{heading:`Admission requirements: Bachelor's programmes`,bullets:[`Class 10 and 12 certificates and transcripts.`,`General and programme-specific entry qualifications recognised by the university admissions system.`,`Required subject prerequisites, particularly for engineering and science.`,`English proficiency meeting the programme's published requirement.`,`Some programmes may have selection tests, portfolios or additional criteria.`]},{heading:`Admission requirements: Master's programmes`,bullets:[`Recognised Bachelor's degree equivalent to the required Swedish level.`,`Relevant subject background and specific course credits, where required.`,`Academic transcripts and degree certificate.`,`English proficiency meeting the programme requirement.`,`CV, statement of purpose, references or portfolio where requested.`],note:`Language requirements vary by institution and course. IELTS, TOEFL or other evidence may be accepted for English-taught programmes. Alternative evidence or waivers are at the institution's discretion; there is no universal waiver.`},{heading:`Tuition fees`,table:{head:[`Study category`,`Indicative annual tuition`],rows:[[`Non-EU Bachelor's programmes`,`Often approximately SEK 80,000–150,000+ per year`],[`Non-EU Master's programmes`,`Often approximately SEK 90,000–200,000+ per year`],[`Scholarships`,`University and Swedish Institute opportunities may be available; eligibility and coverage vary`]]}},{heading:`Cost of living`,table:{head:[`Monthly expense`,`Indicative cost`],rows:[[`Accommodation`,`SEK 4,000–8,000`],[`Food and groceries`,`SEK 2,500–3,500`],[`Transport`,`SEK 600–1,000`],[`Personal / study expenses`,`SEK 1,000–2,000`],[`Indicative monthly total`,`SEK 10,000–15,000`]]},note:`Estimated annual planning budget — A broad planning estimate is around SEK 210,000–380,000+ per year including tuition and living costs. Programme fees, city, accommodation and exchange rates affect the final amount. Treat this as a starting estimate and request the latest fee schedule from the institution.`},{heading:`Student visa / residence requirements for Indian students`,paras:[`Non-EU students planning to study in Sweden for more than three months generally need a residence permit for higher education before travelling. Students normally need full-time admission, paid tuition where applicable and proof of maintenance funds meeting the Swedish Migration Agency's current threshold. Apply early and follow the official checklist.`,`Common documents may include:`],bullets:[`Valid passport and copies of relevant pages.`,`Final admission decision for eligible full-time studies.`,`Proof of tuition fee payment where required before the permit decision.`,`Proof of maintenance funds for the required period, meeting the current threshold.`,`Comprehensive health insurance where required for the duration of the stay.`,`Any additional documents requested by the Swedish Migration Agency.`],note:`Visa and immigration reminder — The final checklist depends on nationality, course duration, institution and current immigration rules. Use the official government or embassy checklist and the university's international office instructions. Check translation, apostille/legalisation, insurance, financial threshold and appointment rules before submission.`},{heading:`Part-time work and post-study options`,bullets:[`A student with a valid Swedish residence permit for higher education is generally allowed to work alongside studies without a separate work permit; academic progress and permit conditions remain important.`,`Students must maintain the conditions for their residence permit and should not rely on employment to meet the initial financial-maintenance requirement.`,`Graduates may be eligible to apply for a residence permit to look for work or explore starting a business, subject to current requirements.`]},{heading:`Frequently asked questions`,points:[{title:`Are there English-taught courses in Sweden?`,text:`Yes. There are many English-taught Master's programmes and a smaller selection of Bachelor's programmes. Check the official programme database for current availability.`},{title:`Can students work while studying in Sweden?`,text:`Students with the relevant higher-education residence permit are generally allowed to work, but must continue meeting their study and permit conditions.`},{title:`Are scholarships available?`,text:`Some universities and the Swedish Institute offer scholarships for eligible international students. Coverage, nationality criteria and deadlines differ.`}]}],closing:{heading:`Is Sweden right for you?`,paras:[`Sweden may suit students interested in research, technology, engineering, sustainability and collaborative learning, with a budget that can accommodate tuition and relatively high living costs.`,`HN Overseas can support profile assessment, course and university shortlisting, application documentation, scholarship research, visa-document preparation and pre-departure planning.`]}},mauritius:{key:`mauritius`,slug:`study-in-mauritius`,kicker:`Study destinations · Mauritius`,h1:`Study in Mauritius`,lead:`A multicultural island destination with regional and international study opportunities. Mauritius offers a mix of public and private higher education institutions and is known regionally for programmes in business, management, information technology, hospitality, tourism and selected professional fields. Its multicultural environment and use of English and French in education and daily life can appeal to students seeking an alternative study destination. Applicants should check institutional accreditation and professional recognition carefully, especially for regulated courses.`,heroImg:{src:v,src768:w,alt:`Students in a seminar room at a university campus`,w:1200,h:800},sections:[{heading:`Why study in Mauritius?`,bullets:[`Multicultural environment with English and French widely used.`,`Study options in business, IT, hospitality, tourism and selected professional fields.`,`A range of public and private institutions.`,`Regional links with Africa, Asia and international business.`,`Potentially different cost profile from major European study destinations.`]},{heading:`Education system and study pattern`,paras:[`Mauritius has universities and other tertiary education providers offering undergraduate, postgraduate and professional qualifications. Programme length, academic calendar, assessment and recognition depend on the institution and course.`],table:{head:[`Qualification`,`Typical duration`],rows:[[`Bachelor's degree`,`Often 3 years; some programmes longer`],[`Master's degree`,`Often 1–2 years`],[`Doctoral degree`,`Varies by research area and institution`]]}},{heading:`Popular courses`,bullets:[`Business Administration and Management`,`Accounting, Finance and Economics`,`Information Technology and Computer Science`,`Hospitality and Tourism Management`,`Marketing and International Business`,`Selected health, science and professional programmes`,`Logistics and Supply Chain Management`]},{heading:`Universities to explore`,paras:[`These institutions are starting points for research, not a ranking. Check current programme availability, campus, language of instruction, accreditation and entry requirements on the official website.`],table:{head:[`Institution`,`Key study areas`,`Official website`],rows:[[(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.uom.ac.mu/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`University of Mauritius`}),`Business, science, engineering, law and humanities`,(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.uom.ac.mu/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`https://www.uom.ac.mu/`})],[(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.utm.ac.mu/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`University of Technology, Mauritius`}),`Technology, business, health and applied disciplines`,(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.utm.ac.mu/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`https://www.utm.ac.mu/`})],[(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.middlesex.mu/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`Middlesex University Mauritius`}),`Business, psychology, IT and related programmes`,(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.middlesex.mu/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`https://www.middlesex.mu/`})],[(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://curtinmauritius.ac.mu/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`Curtin Mauritius`}),`Business, IT and related programmes`,(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://curtinmauritius.ac.mu/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`https://curtinmauritius.ac.mu/`})],[(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.open.ac.mu/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`Open University of Mauritius`}),`Flexible and distance-learning programmes across disciplines`,(0,T.jsx)(`a`,{href:`https://www.open.ac.mu/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener`,children:`https://www.open.ac.mu/`})]]}},{heading:`Admission requirements: Bachelor's programmes`,bullets:[`Class 10 and 12 certificates and transcripts.`,`Secondary qualification meeting the institution's programme entry requirements.`,`Required subject background and grades for the selected course.`,`English or French language evidence where required.`,`Additional selection, interview or professional requirements for selected programmes.`]},{heading:`Admission requirements: Master's programmes`,bullets:[`Recognised Bachelor's degree in a relevant discipline.`,`Degree certificate and academic transcripts.`,`CV and statement of purpose where requested.`,`English or French language evidence as required.`,`Relevant work experience or professional registration for selected programmes.`],note:`Language requirements vary by institution and course. IELTS, TOEFL or other evidence may be accepted for English-taught programmes. Alternative evidence or waivers are at the institution's discretion; there is no universal waiver.`},{heading:`Tuition fees`,table:{head:[`Study category`,`Indicative annual tuition`],rows:[[`Undergraduate programmes`,`Indicatively around MUR 100,000–300,000+ per year; institution and programme dependent`],[`Postgraduate programmes`,`Indicatively around MUR 120,000–350,000+ per year; varies widely`],[`Specialist / professional courses`,`May be substantially higher; request the official fee schedule`]]}},{heading:`Cost of living`,table:{head:[`Monthly expense`,`Indicative cost`],rows:[[`Accommodation`,`MUR 8,000–18,000`],[`Food and groceries`,`MUR 6,000–10,000`],[`Transport`,`MUR 1,500–3,000`],[`Personal expenses`,`MUR 3,000–6,000`],[`Indicative monthly total`,`MUR 18,500–37,000`]]},note:`Estimated annual planning budget — A preliminary annual planning range for tuition and living may be around MUR 322,000–744,000+ for some programmes. This is a broad guide only; housing, institution, insurance and course type can change the total significantly. Treat this as a starting estimate and request the latest fee schedule from the institution.`},{heading:`Student visa / residence requirements for Indian students`,paras:[`International students need the appropriate student visa/residence authorisation before or upon arrival according to the current Mauritian immigration procedure. The institution generally provides admission documentation and guidance for the application. Students should confirm the exact process, financial evidence, medical and insurance requirements with the Passport and Immigration Office and the institution.`,`Common documents may include:`],bullets:[`Valid passport and completed application forms.`,`Official admission letter from an eligible institution.`,`Evidence of tuition payment or financial arrangements, as required.`,`Proof of sufficient funds and sponsor documents, if applicable.`,`Accommodation details and return/onward travel information if requested.`,`Medical examination, health insurance or other health documents if required.`,`Academic certificates, photographs and any additional immigration documents.`],note:`Visa and immigration reminder — The final checklist depends on nationality, course duration, institution and current immigration rules. Use the official government or embassy checklist and the university's international office instructions. Check translation, apostille/legalisation, insurance, financial threshold and appointment rules before submission.`},{heading:`Part-time work and post-study options`,bullets:[`Student employment is not automatic; permission and conditions depend on the student's immigration status and current Mauritian rules.`,`Students must obtain confirmation from the institution and immigration authorities before undertaking paid work.`,`Post-study employment requires the appropriate work and residence authorisation; do not assume an automatic post-study work route.`]},{heading:`Frequently asked questions`,points:[{title:`Are programmes in Mauritius taught in English?`,text:`Many institutions use English as a principal language of instruction, while French is also widely used. Confirm the teaching language for the exact course.`},{title:`Is Mauritius a low-cost study destination?`,text:`Costs vary by institution, accommodation and lifestyle. Compare the full annual cost and not just tuition before making a decision.`},{title:`Can international students work in Mauritius?`,text:`Work permission is subject to immigration rules and the student's status. Obtain written, current guidance before planning to work.`}]}],closing:{heading:`Is Mauritius right for you?`,paras:[`Mauritius may suit students seeking a multicultural environment and programmes in business, IT or hospitality, particularly where the institution and qualification have been carefully checked for recognition and career relevance.`,`HN Overseas can support profile assessment, course and university shortlisting, application documentation, scholarship research, visa-document preparation and pre-departure planning.`]}},australia:E,canada:D,dubai:O,europe:k,nz:A,uk:j,usa:M,mba:N,about:P,payment:F,refund:I,privacy:L,terms:R,faq:{key:`faq`,slug:`faq`,kicker:`Frequently asked questions`,h1:`Questions families ask us`,lead:`The questions that come up at almost every first meeting, answered the way we answer them in the office — and the rest of what families ask us before they start, grouped by topic.`,sections:[],faqGroups:[{heading:`Counselling & costs`,items:[{q:`How much does counselling cost?`,a:`Counselling is free for every country, including Italy. For most countries our application help is also free — you only pay the university's own application fee, if it charges one, directly to the university. Ivy League applications are charged per application. Italy has one full process fee covering everything from scratch to the visa, including applications to up to three universities, with a 100% scholarship guaranteed for eligible students. Small official charges such as the visa fee, HRD attestation and registration are paid by you separately. Any fee that applies is confirmed in writing before you commit.`},{q:`Who will guide me?`,a:`HN Overseas has guided students for 35+ years, since 1985, as part of the Career Point family — 3,500+ students counselled, 1,500+ universities across 41+ countries. Your counselling is led by a mentor who is British Council Certified, with 10+ years of experience and 4,000+ students counselled, and the team stays with you from the first conversation to your arrival.`}]},{heading:`Countries & intakes`,items:[{q:`Which countries can I study in?`,a:`We guide students for Italy, the USA, the UK, Canada, Australia, Ireland, the UAE (Dubai), New Zealand and Singapore — and for Hungary and Malta inside Europe — and, through our wider network, for 41+ countries and 1,500+ universities in all. The guides on this site go deep on the countries families ask about most.`},{q:`When are the intakes, and when should I apply?`,a:`It differs by country. USA: Fall, Spring and Summer. UK: September and January, with May for some postgraduate courses. Canada: September, January and May. Australia: February, July and November. Ireland: September, with January for some postgraduate courses. UAE: September, January and May. New Zealand: February, July and November. Singapore: August and January. Italy has a single September intake. Whichever country you choose, starting early matters — most families miss scholarships only because they start late.`},{q:`Can I work part-time while I study?`,a:`In most destinations, yes, within set hours. Australia allows up to 24 hours a week in term time and full-time work in the holidays. The UK and New Zealand allow up to 20 hours a week in term time and full-time in the breaks. In Canada you can work part-time during your studies and full-time during scheduled breaks, and many programmes include a co-op — a paid placement linked to your field. Italy's rules are covered in the Italy section below.`},{q:`Can I stay back after my degree?`,a:`Most destinations offer a post-study route. Australia's Temporary Graduate Visa (Subclass 485) allows two to four years, depending on your qualification and where you study. Canada's Post-Graduation Work Permit can run for up to three years. The UK Graduate Route gives two years after an undergraduate or Master's degree, and up to three years after a PhD. New Zealand allows up to three years, depending on the level of your qualification. Italy offers a 1-year post-study stay-back.`}]},{heading:`Scholarships`,items:[{q:`Can I get a scholarship in Italy?`,a:`Yes, if you are eligible. Need based regional scholarships pay about 7,000 to 8,000 euros a year as a stipend, and public universities charge little or no tuition on top of that.`},{q:`Are there scholarships outside Italy?`,a:`Yes — every destination has its own funding. Australia's government and universities offer scholarships that help with tuition, living expenses and sometimes travel. Canada offers scholarships and grants based on academic performance, research interests and leadership. New Zealand's universities and government offer merit-based undergraduate awards and research grants for postgraduates. US colleges award substantial scholarships, research assistantships and merit-based aid. Whatever you are eligible for, we check it and apply alongside your admission.`}]},{heading:`Studying in Italy`,items:[{q:`How much does Italy cost overall?`,a:`3 to 3.5 lakh rupees for a Bachelor's or Master's degree, and 4 to 4.5 lakh rupees for MBBS. The visa fund is separate from those totals: it is money you must show in your bank account for the visa — you don't pay it to us or to the university.`},{q:`Can I work while studying?`,a:`In Italy, yes. You can work 20 hours a week during your studies and full time in the holidays, and a 1 year post study work visa follows your degree.`},{q:`What is the visa fund?`,a:`The visa fund is separate from the Italy totals above: it is money you must show in your bank account for the visa — you don't pay it to us or to the university. It is proof of funds for your visa application, not a charge, and it stays in your account.`},{q:`Do I need IELTS for Italy?`,a:`For most Italian public universities, no. Most accept a Medium of Instruction (MOI) certificate from your school or college instead of an English test score. Whether your profile and your chosen university need one is confirmed by your counsellor in the free counselling session.`}]},{heading:`Applications & documents`,items:[{q:`How does the process work, step by step?`,a:`Seven steps. First, free counselling: we sit with you and your parents, look at your marks and your budget, and say plainly which countries and courses fit. Second, test preparation, planned early if your universities ask for a test. Third, shortlisting — from more than 1,500 partner universities we narrow your options to a list that matches your grades, subjects and budget. Fourth, applications and SOPs, built with you, with every document and deadline kept in one place. Fifth, scholarships, checked and applied for alongside your admission. Sixth, your visa file, prepared document by document, with interview practice. Seventh, pre-departure and arrival support — housing, money and your first week — and we stay in touch after you land.`},{q:`What documents will I need?`,a:`Generally: your passport, marksheets and transcripts, an English test score (IELTS or TOEFL) or an MOI certificate where one is accepted, a statement of purpose, recommendation letters, a CV and financial documents. The exact list depends on the country and the university, so your counsellor confirms the final checklist in your free counselling session.`}]},{heading:`Visas`,items:[{q:`What are the visa chances?`,a:`Our visa success rate is 98%. When students follow our documentation and guidance, that rate sits between 96 and 98%.`},{q:`Can anyone guarantee my visa?`,a:`No — and be wary of anyone who promises one. The decision is always the embassy's. What we can say is that when students follow our documentation and guidance, our visa success rate sits between 96 and 98%. Correct paperwork is exactly where we help most: your visa file is prepared document by document, and we practise the interview with you until your answers are calm, honest and clear.`}]},{heading:`Payments & refunds`,items:[{q:`How do I pay, and will my payment be documented?`,a:`We accept UPI (PhonePe, Google Pay and Paytm), bank transfer (NEFT/IMPS), credit or debit card via a payment portal, and cash at authorised HN Overseas offices only. We issue a formal invoice and receipt for every transaction, including GST where it applies. Before you send any money, verify the payment details with your counsellor — HN Overseas is not responsible for payments made to people or agents who are not authorised by us.`},{q:`What if I withdraw, or my visa is refused — can I get a refund?`,a:`Our Refund Policy covers the services we charge for — counselling itself is always free. If you withdraw before any work has started, you can receive a 90% refund; 10% goes towards administrative costs. If services have partly been provided, a pro-rated refund may be given for the portion not used. If every university on your shortlist rejects you, and it is not because documents were not sent or you were not eligible, you may be able to receive a 50% refund, depending on the stage your process had reached. If your visa is denied after our team reviewed your application and documents, and the rejection is not because of any false information, we may refund 30% of the fee. To request a refund, email business.hnoverseas@gmail.com within 15 days of cancelling or receiving the rejection notice; we review requests within 5 to 7 business days and, if approved, refund to your original payment method within 10 to 15 business days. The full policy is on our Refund Policy page.`}]},{heading:`Test preparation`,items:[{q:`Is IELTS compulsory?`,a:`For most universities, no. IELTS is mandatory for only a few, and most accept a Medium of Instruction certificate from your school or college instead. One thing is fixed: the visa process requires a B2 level English certificate.`},{q:`Do you offer test preparation?`,a:`Yes — coaching for GRE, GMAT, SAT, IELTS, TOEFL and PTE. Test preparation is a paid service, priced by course and confirmed with you before you enrol. If your chosen universities ask for a test, we plan your preparation early, so your scores are ready well before application deadlines.`}]}]},testprep:{key:`testprep`,slug:`test-prep`,kicker:`Test preparation`,h1:`Test preparation`,lead:`Some universities ask for a test score alongside your application. We offer coaching for IELTS, TOEFL, GRE, GMAT, SAT and PTE — planned early with your counsellor, so your scores are ready well before application deadlines. Counselling is completely free; test preparation is a paid service, priced by course and confirmed with you before you enrol.`,sections:[{heading:`The tests we prepare you for`,points:[{id:`ielts`,title:`IELTS`,text:`English-language preparation for the universities that ask for an IELTS score. Many universities accept a Medium of Instruction certificate instead — your counsellor confirms which route your shortlist needs, free, before you enrol.`},{id:`toefl`,title:`TOEFL`,text:`English-language preparation for the universities that ask for a TOEFL score — one of the two English tests named in most document checklists, alongside IELTS.`},{id:`gre`,title:`GRE`,text:`Preparation for the GRE, which graduate programmes may ask for as part of your application — planned early, so the score is ready well before your deadlines.`},{id:`gmat`,title:`GMAT`,text:`Preparation for the GMAT, which business schools may ask for with MBA and management applications — planned early, so the score is ready well before your deadlines.`},{id:`sat`,title:`SAT`,text:`Preparation for the SAT, which undergraduate programmes may ask for as part of your application — planned early, so the score is ready well before your deadlines.`},{id:`pte`,title:`PTE`,text:`English-language preparation for the universities that ask for a PTE score — planned early with your counsellor, so the result is ready well before your application deadlines.`}]},{heading:`Questions about test preparation`,points:[{title:`Is IELTS compulsory?`,text:`For most universities, no. IELTS is mandatory for only a few, and most accept a Medium of Instruction certificate from your school or college instead. One thing is fixed: the visa process requires a B2 level English certificate.`},{title:`Do you offer test preparation?`,text:`Yes — coaching for GRE, GMAT, SAT, IELTS, TOEFL and PTE. Test preparation is a paid service, priced by course and confirmed with you before you enrol. If your chosen universities ask for a test, we plan your preparation early, so your scores are ready well before application deadlines.`}]}]}};export{z as t};